-3","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Die Kapitel, die das Entwicklungsteam verantworten kann: Schwellwertanalyse, Verfahren und\nTechnik, Rechtsgrundlagen, Betroffenenrechte, Ergebnis. Jede code-gestützte Aussage trägt ihren\nBeleg mit Repository, Pfad und Zeilenbereich."},"6":{"id":"/-4","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/","content":"Die plattformweite ADR-Reihe 001–023. Die DSFA verweist auf sie; jede Nennung im Text ist\nverlinkt."},"7":{"id":"/-5","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#drei-regeln-nach-denen-die-texte-geschrieben-sind","content":"**Was nicht live ist, wird nicht als vorhanden beschrieben.** Der Status jedes Belegs\n(`live`, `standardmäßig aus`, `nicht ausgeliefert`, `Live-Prüfung offen`) steht neben der Aussage."},"8":{"id":"/-6","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#drei-regeln-nach-denen-die-texte-geschrieben-sind","content":"**Risiko benennen, Kompensation sofort nachschieben.**"},"9":{"id":"/-7","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#drei-regeln-nach-denen-die-texte-geschrieben-sind","content":"**Grenzen ehrlich benennen.** „Beinahe unmöglich\", „nicht haltbar\", „darf nicht behauptet werden\"\nsind Absicht."},"10":{"id":"/-8","page_id":"/","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/#wie-die-belege-funktionieren","content":"Unter jedem technischen Abschnitt liegt ein Block &#x2A;*„Belege aus dem Code\"**. „Code anzeigen\" öffnet\nden Quelltext aus dem Understand-Anything-Knowledge-Graphen mit hervorgehobenem Zeilenbereich;\n„GitHub\" führt auf denselben Pfad im Repository. Die Belegtabelle selbst liegt maschinenlesbar in\n`oriso-platform/dsfa-text/evidence-map.yaml`."},"11":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"page","content":"ADR-001: Counselling modalities as toggleable modules","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001"},"12":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001","content":"Status: Proposed — needs a team decision (esp. how registration filters on `consultingtype`) · Datum: 2026-06-23"},"13":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"Context"},"14":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#requirement-product","content":"Requirement (product)"},"15":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-drivers","content":"Decision drivers"},"16":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"Decision (proposed)"},"17":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"18":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#migration-plan-incremental-no-big-bang","content":"Migration plan (incremental, no big bang)"},"19":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#open-questions-need-a-decision","content":"Open questions (need a decision)"},"20":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-001#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"21":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001","content":"**Status:** Proposed — needs a team decision (esp. how registration filters on `consulting_type`)"},"22":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-23"},"23":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + backend/frontend leads"},"24":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001","content":"**Related:** OpenResilienceInitiative/ORISO-Frontend#245, ORISO-AgencyService#39 (wipe fix), ORISO-Frontend#246 (hide empty topics), ORISO-AgencyService#40 (data cleanup), `agency-registration-visibility-bug-report.md`"},"25":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"`consulting_type` is the most overloaded concept in the platform. Today it simultaneously is:"},"26":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"**the modality / channel identity** — live/proximity chat, 1:1, internal chat, soon self-help-group chat, future video (confirmed: `/service/consultingtypes/basic` carries `groupChat.isGroupChat`, `isVideoCallAllowed`, `isAnonymousConversationAllowed`, `isSubsequentRegistrationAllowed`, …);"},"27":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"**a hard filter in registration** — `AgencyRepository.search*` enforces `a.consulting_type = :type`, and the frontend hardcodes `consultingType: consultingType?.id || 1` (`useAgenciesForRegistration.ts`). Any agency whose modality ≠ the hardcoded value is silently dropped;"},"28":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"**a carrier of per-type feature settings** (group chat rules, video allowed, anonymous, mandatory registration fields, white-spot, …)."},"29":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"On top of that:"},"30":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"**Topics** carry the subject (\"Anliegen\"); they live in ConsultingTypeService, are **tenant-scoped** (`tenant_id`), were seeded into prod manually (no changelog), and are referenced from `agency_topic` in **AgencyService with no cross-service FK**."},"31":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"**User journeys diverge sharply.** The async \"enquiry/letter\" flow needs **postcode (geo) routing + topic + a 2-day SLA**. The **live-chat** flow is a **link**, no postcode, a **waiting room**, real-time **agent availability**, and many organisations sharing a pool. Forcing both through one `getAgencies(consultingType, postcode, topicId)` filter is the source of recurring, silent failures."},"32":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#context","content":"A false in-code comment (\"consulting types are not used anymore\") has already produced fragile logic (`getConsultingType4Tenant` assigning a modality via `consultingTypeResponse[0].id`)."},"33":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#requirement-product","content":"Be able to **enable/disable modules** per tenant and per agency — \"this Träger only does live chat, not 1:1\" — and to toggle **per-chat features** (audio messages, file upload, …), like the existing admin toggles. This is a core component and must be hardened so it stops generating errors."},"34":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-drivers","content":"Modules must be **toggleable** per tenant and per agency (and feature-flaggable per modality)."},"35":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-drivers","content":"Different flows have **different routing and availability** semantics (geo+SLA vs link+waiting-room)."},"36":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-drivers","content":"**No silent registration failures** (no hidden hard filter that drops valid agencies)."},"37":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-drivers","content":"**Data integrity** across services (no dangling topic/modality references; versioned seeds)."},"38":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"Model three **orthogonal axes** explicitly and stop conflating them."},"39":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Topic** = subject. &#x2A;*Modality (module)** = delivery channel, owning its own feature flags. **Agency** = provider declaring a capability matrix of `(topic × modality, enabled?)`."},"40":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Capabilities are explicit, toggleable flags** — *not* a single overloaded enum used as a filter. A tenant enables which modalities exist; an agency declares which it offers; each modality carries its feature toggles. (Consistent with the project's \"disable, don't hide\" rule and the planned ADV-module concept.)"},"41":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Each modality gets its own entry flow**, sharing the capability model but not the same filter query:"},"42":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"*Async enquiry*: topic → postcode (geo routing) → agency → message; SLA-driven."},"43":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"*Live chat*: link → optional topic → waiting room; availability/queue-driven; no geo routing; many orgs share the pool."},"44":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Registration must not hardcode or secretly filter modality.** The async flow filters by **topic + postcode + availability**; the modality is implied by the flow (or chosen). The live-chat flow passes its own modality. Never `consultingType = 1` as a constant."},"45":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Harden the data model:** version-controlled seeds (no manual prod seeding); referential integrity or an integrity check across services (no `agency_topic.topic_id` / modality id without a matching definition); reachability validation before an agency can be \"visible in registration\" (online + ≥1 consultant + has the relevant capability); availability/waiting-room modelled as a modality concern."},"46":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#decision-proposed","content":"**Credential invariant:** managed human accounts (platform admins, tenant admins, agency admins, counsellors) must not receive silent/generated random passwords as a hidden fallback. They need an explicit password at creation or a secure reset/invite flow. The exception is registrationless anonymous live chat: that flow intentionally creates a hidden unique technical username plus generated credentials while the visible display name remains non-unique. Those technical credentials are required for the anonymous login/session bridge and must not be removed under the \"no silent random password\" rule."},"47":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#consequences","content":"**Positive:** modules are independently toggleable; flows match their real requirements; no silent drops; new modalities (video, self-help group) become additive instead of breaking the registration filter; data integrity stops the recurring \"agency missing\" class of bug."},"48":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** this is a refactor of a core component. `consulting_type` semantics must be migrated deliberately (it currently carries modality), schema + admin UX work is needed, and the two flows must be split. Coordination across ConsultingTypeService / AgencyService / TenantService / UserService / Frontend."},"49":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#migration-plan-incremental-no-big-bang","content":"**Phase 0 — stop the bleeding (in progress):** fix the destructive topic-link wipe (ORISO-AgencyService#39 ✅), hide empty topics in registration (ORISO-Frontend#246 ✅), clean up broken test agencies (ORISO-AgencyService#40), and **decide the registration `consultingType` handling** (see open question)."},"50":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#migration-plan-incremental-no-big-bang","content":"**Phase 1 — model capabilities explicitly:** introduce per-tenant/per-agency modality toggles + per-modality feature flags; remove the `[0].id` modality assignment and the false \"deprecated\" comment; make modality an explicit, validated field in the agency form."},"51":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#migration-plan-incremental-no-big-bang","content":"**Phase 2 — split flows:** give live chat its own entry/flow (link + waiting room + availability) distinct from the async enquiry flow; stop sharing the single agency filter."},"52":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#migration-plan-incremental-no-big-bang","content":"**Phase 3 — data integrity:** version-control topic/modality seeds; add cross-service integrity checks; reachability validation on \"visible in registration\"."},"53":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#open-questions-need-a-decision","content":"**Registration filter:** for the async flow, send the real modality, or send none and filter by topic + availability only (backend already supports `:type IS NULL`)? Since the type now carries modality, this is a product decision, not a pure code one."},"54":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#open-questions-need-a-decision","content":"**Where does modality config live** — ConsultingTypeService (today), TenantService, or a dedicated capability model?"},"55":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#open-questions-need-a-decision","content":"**Availability model for live chat** — queue/waiting-room + agent presence: new component or extend an existing service?"},"56":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#alternatives-considered","content":"**Keep `consulting_type` as-is, just stop hardcoding `=1`.** Cheapest, but leaves the overload (identity + filter + features) and the divergent-flows problem; the silent-failure class will recur as modalities grow."},"57":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#alternatives-considered","content":"**Drop modality filtering entirely in registration.** Simpler, but then registration can offer modalities a Träger doesn't actually provide — wrong for the toggle requirement."},"58":{"id":"/decisions/adr-001-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-001","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-001#alternatives-considered","content":"**Proposed (three axes + capabilities + per-flow):** highest upfront cost, but the only option that satisfies the toggle requirement and the divergent flows without recurring breakage."},"59":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"page","content":"ADR-002: Silent room membership with an access-control confidentiality curtain (not E2EE)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002"},"60":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending) · Datum: 2026-06-25"},"61":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"Context"},"62":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"Decision"},"63":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"64":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"65":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"Relationship to the in-flight Case Handover work (cross-checked 2026-06-25)"},"66":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"Reveal lifecycle (decided 2026-06-25)"},"67":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"Resolved (design session 2026-06-25)"},"68":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-002#implementation-notes-added-2026-07-30-after-905-made-1-live","content":"Implementation notes (added 2026-07-30, after #905 made §1 live)"},"69":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending)"},"70":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-25"},"71":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + backend/Matrix/frontend leads"},"72":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002","content":"**Related:** ADR-001 (modalities as modules); `ORISO-UserService/CONTEXT.md`; `ORISO-Frontend/CONTEXT.md` (Handover); UserService `UnauthorizedMembersProvider`, `AgencyPreAssignmentRoomService`, `AssignEnquiryFacade`, `MatrixRoomClient`, `SessionSupervisorFacade`"},"73":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"A client conversation is a Matrix room. Two things are broken / unsettled today:"},"74":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"**The Rocket.Chat-era membership model is \"invite the whole agency, then the\naccepting counsellor kicks everyone else\"** (`UnauthorizedMembersProvider`). The\nMatrix migration never settled a replacement — the Matrix path instead creates an\nagency-service-account \"holding room\" with only the client, then invites a single\nconsultant on accept. A counsellor who steps in later (e.g. covering for a sick\ncolleague) therefore **joins late**."},"75":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"**There is no confidentiality boundary at all.** Verified on Pre-Dev: Synapse runs\nwith no encryption config (rooms unencrypted, message content plaintext in\n`homeserver.db`) and no `history_visibility` override (`private_chat` preset →\n`shared`), so **any member who joins reads the full prior history**. The frontend's\nE2EE is still the Rocket.Chat scheme, which skips Matrix rooms entirely."},"76":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"Product need: every counsellor in a department should be reachable to *cover* a case,\nincluding taking over a sick colleague's active case **with its history** — but an\noff-case counsellor must not casually see cases they aren't handling."},"77":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#context","content":"Given \"real members from creation,\" at most two of these three can hold: a\n**cryptographic** curtain, **reveal-grants-history**, and **no key-redistribution\nevent**. We must pick."},"78":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"**Scope:** this applies to the **one-to-one (nearby / proximity) counselling** chat type only.\nLive chat (ephemeral, single counsellor, no look-in) and internal chat are out of scope."},"79":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"**1. Real members from room creation (no invite-then-kick, no late join).**\nWhen a conversation is created, the relevant department's counsellors are *genuinely*\njoined to the room as **silent members** (building on the existing team-session\nmechanism). The handling counsellor is the **active counsellor**; the rest remain\nsilent. \"Reveal\" is a visibility/permission flip on an existing membership — nobody\never joins late, so there is no re-key / history-replay problem."},"80":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"**2. The curtain is access-control / UX, not cryptographic (relax the crypto property).**\nSilent members technically *can* read (rooms stay effectively unencrypted, or keys\nflow to all members); \"silent\" means the client app **hides** the conversation and\n**mutes** notifications. Real confidentiality is enforced by:"},"81":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"**department-scoped search** — a counsellor can only discover clients/conversations/\ncounsellors within their own department(s), never outside their scope;"},"82":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"the **apply-to-reveal gate** — making a hidden conversation visible is a deliberate act;"},"83":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"an **audit log of every reveal** — who revealed which case, when, on what basis."},"84":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#decision","content":"**Reveal grants full prior history** (continuity of care for takeover). Plaintext-at-rest\nis mitigated by **disk/volume encryption**, not message E2EE."},"85":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#consequences","content":"**Positive:** sick-colleague takeover \"just works\" (the colleague was already a member);\nno late-join key/history breakage; the half-finished Matrix migration gets a definite\ntarget model; replaces the brittle invite-then-kick."},"86":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** there is **no cryptographic confidentiality between counsellors of\nthe same agency** — a determined same-agency counsellor's client could read a case they\nhaven't revealed. Security now **rests entirely on scoped search + the reveal gate +\naudit**, so those become load-bearing controls that must be correct and tamper-evident.\nMessage content remains plaintext server-side until disk encryption is in place."},"87":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#alternatives-considered","content":"**Real Matrix E2EE + share historical keys on reveal** (relax \"no key event\"): a true\nboundary against colleagues *and* continuity, but a substantial build (replace the dead\nRocket.Chat E2EE) and reintroduces a key-distribution event at reveal time."},"88":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#alternatives-considered","content":"**Real E2EE, forward-only reveal** (relax \"history on reveal\"): true boundary + cheap,\nbut the covering colleague cannot read what the client already said — breaks the core\nscenario."},"89":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#alternatives-considered","content":"**Shadow membership, reveal = real join** (reject Option A): reproduces exactly the\nlate-join history/re-key bug this ADR removes."},"90":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"This ADR is the same decision the **Case Handover (Fallübergabe) KDG-compliant** epic\n(`CAR-CHO-01`) reached independently: separate **technical eligibility** from\n**justified visibility**, discard key-escrow. Built so far (PRs UserService #186,\nFrontend #275, Admin #208, Database #13 merged): the **policy-gate + reason +\nexplanation + client-consent + audit + admin-config + content-locked gate** slice."},"91":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"**Not yet built / divergent from this ADR:**"},"92":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"**Technical eligibility is assumed, not implemented** — `CaseHandoverService.requestAccess`\ngrants via `session.setConsultant(requester)` and never establishes Matrix room\nmembership; it only works because rooms are currently unencrypted. ADR-002's \"real\nmembers from creation\" has no implementation. &#x2A;*Decided 2026-06-25 (Frank): build this\nmembership layer now as the next slice (department joins each conversation at creation),\nnot defer it to the future spike.**"},"93":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"**Grant = single-owner transfer for every reason** (even \"asked for advice\"), rather\nthan optionally adding a co-active counsellor."},"94":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"**`case_handover_reason_policy` is global** (PK `code`, no `tenant_id`) and only models\n`client_consent_required` + `access_allowed` — so platform-default → tenant-override →\nread-only pass-down, and the Client/Counsellor/Supervisor/Law-Enforcement approval\nmatrix, are not representable yet."},"95":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#relationship-to-the-in-flight-case-handover-work-cross-checked-2026-06-25","content":"**Scope is agency + non-team-sessions**, not Department (agency × topic) + team sessions."},"96":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"Governing invariant: **membership ≠ visibility** — the whole department are silent members\n(technical eligibility) but see nothing; only a small, deliberately revealed, time-boxed,\nlogged set watches a case. Two reveal flavours over one primitive, chosen by the reason's\n**access outcome**:"},"97":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"**Co-access** (advice/consult): read-only, time-boxed peek that **auto-expires** (re-lock +\naudit entry); original keeps full visibility; no ownership change. Reuses the **Supervision**\nprimitive + a new auto-expiry timer + self-service gate."},"98":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"**Takeover** (absence reasons): cover gains full visibility and ownership; original is\nre-hidden but keeps membership and can **reclaim**; no auto-expiry (until reclaim/return)."},"99":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"**Reclaim**: reverse of takeover; permanent reasons (\"left\") have no reclaim."},"100":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#reveal-lifecycle-decided-2026-06-25","content":"TTL: a per-reason `max_access_duration` (co-access default \\~3h, tenant-configurable; takeover =\n`null` = until reclaim). &#x2A;*Audit scope: per-agency, visible to the tenant (agency/tenant admins +\nDPO), not the platform owner.** The merged `case_handover_request` table already carries\n`tenant_id`; only `case_handover_reason_policy` still lacks it."},"101":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"**Reveal gate** = a configurable per-reason **handover policy** (Admin); two **access\noutcomes** — *co-access* (read-only, time-boxed, auto-expiry; original keeps sight) and\n*takeover* (full + ownership, original re-hidden but keeps membership, **reclaimable**;\n\"left\" = no reclaim). An **absent** colleague's case is taken over via the away-reason itself\n(no consent from the absent person); reclaim on return."},"102":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"**Department (agency × topic)** is first-class and carries imprint/DPP — see **ADR-003**."},"103":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"**Contractual basis** binds at conversation creation (nearby → its Department; live → the\ninvite-link Department), snapshotted + immutable; draft/unpublished basis = record-only."},"104":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"**Policy storage** = config owned in **TenantService** (platform defaults + tenant overrides +\nread-only pass-down), **cached + enforced in UserService** (Option B). The merged\n`case_handover_reason_policy` becomes the UserService enforcement cache and needs `tenant_id` +\nthe richer approval/outcome/duration fields."},"105":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#resolved-design-session-2026-06-25","content":"**Client visibility** = the client sees only the active counsellor; silent members are\nfiltered from the client view and pseudonymous; disclosure rides the Department DPP."},"106":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#implementation-notes-added-2026-07-30-after-905-made-1-live","content":"**The 1:1 client view derives participants from session data, never from Matrix room\nmembership.** Verified on `pre-dev`: the asker's header resolves from the session `contact`,\nand `useMatrixRoomUsers` is consumed only by group-chat views and mention resolution. Any\nfuture 1:1 view that renders the member list (participant list, read-receipt avatars,\nmembership-derived typing indicator) breaks the curtain — treat that as the invariant."},"107":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#implementation-notes-added-2026-07-30-after-905-made-1-live","content":"**Pseudonymity has to hold at the homeserver, not only in the UI.** The advice seeker is a\nmember of the same room, so their own client can read every member's `displayname` from\n`/joined_members`. Counsellor accounts are therefore provisioned through\n`ConsultantDisplayNameResolver`, which never uses the real name (US#929)."},"108":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#implementation-notes-added-2026-07-30-after-905-made-1-live","content":"**Reveal never adds or removes a member.** A takeover keeps the previous counsellor joined so\nthey can reclaim; a grant tolerates the requester already being a member. Removing a member\nmakes their history unrecoverable under Megolm, and inviting an already-joined member fails\nwith `403 M_FORBIDDEN` — both were live faults in `CaseHandoverService` until US#929."},"109":{"id":"/decisions/adr-002-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-002","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-002#implementation-notes-added-2026-07-30-after-905-made-1-live","content":"**\"Hidden\" is enforced server-side and already was:** the consultant session list is\ndatabase-driven (`consultant IS NULL` for enquiries, `findByConsultant…` once assigned), so an\naccepted case leaves every other counsellor's list without any Matrix action."},"110":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"page","content":"ADR-003: Department = unique (Agency × Topic) carrying its own imprint + DPP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003"},"111":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending) · Datum: 2026-06-25"},"112":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"Context"},"113":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#decision","content":"Decision"},"114":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"115":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"116":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-01","content":"Implementation status (2026-07-01)"},"117":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-03","content":"Implementation status (2026-07-03)"},"118":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-07","content":"Implementation status (2026-07-07)"},"119":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"> **⚠️ Partially superseded by ADR-014 (2026-07-16).** Decision #3 (admin single-select\n> topic picker) is REVERSED: one Beratungsstelle hosts several Fachbereiche, the admin\n> topic picker is multi-select again, and legal texts are shareable `legal_text` objects\n> (`dpp_id`/`imprint_id`). The UNIQUE(agency\\_id, topic\\_id) constraint and per-department\n> imprint/DPP from this ADR remain in force. Read ADR-014 before acting on this document.\n>\n> **Also extended by `ADR-021` (2026-08-16).** The level ladder described here stops at the Träger;\n> there is a platform level above it (main tenant, gated by\n> `legalContentChangesBySingleTenantAdminsAllowed`). Legal texts also have no version history yet —\n> `ADR-021` decides to build one generically. `ADR-022` covers when these documents are shown and\n> how a help-seeker's agreement is recorded."},"120":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending)"},"121":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-25"},"122":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + backend/admin leads"},"123":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003","content":"**Related:** ADR-001 (modalities as modules — topic/agency/modality orthogonal);\nADR-002 (silent membership); `ORISO-UserService/CONTEXT.md`; AgencyService `Agency`,\n`agency_topic`; TenantService `tenant.content_impressum` / `content_privacy`;\n`CentralDataProtectionTemplateService`"},"124":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"A \"department\" (e.g. *Debt counselling*, *Suicide prevention*, *Pregnancy&#x2A; inside one\nagency centre) is, in the domain diagram, an &#x2A;*(agency × topic)** pairing that must carry\nits **own individualised imprint and data privacy policy**, because economically several\ndepartments work \"under one roof\" but are legally distinct."},"125":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"Today in code:"},"126":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"`agency_topic` is a plain join with &#x2A;*no `UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)`** → the same topic\ncan be linked to one agency multiple times (\"duplicate topics\"), which breaks any per-pair\nimprint/DPP mapping and makes routing ambiguous."},"127":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"**Imprint is per-tenant only** (`tenant.content_impressum`); **DPP is per-tenant content\nrendered with per-agency contact placeholders** (`CentralDataProtectionTemplateService`).\nNeither can be individualised per department."},"128":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#context","content":"The silent-membership routing (ADR-002) needs a clean \"topic → the one department → its\ncounsellors + its imprint/DPP\"."},"129":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#decision","content":"**Department is the first-class unit** = a **unique** (agency\\_id, topic\\_id). Enforce\n`UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)`. Duplicate (agency, topic) becomes a **prevented data\nerror**, not a supported case."},"130":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#decision","content":"**Attach `imprint_id` + `dpp_id` to the department**, individualised per pairing\n(overriding/extending the tenant-level imprint and agency-rendered DPP)."},"131":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#decision","content":"**Admin topic picker becomes single-select** (was multi-select). Existing duplicate\n`agency_topic` rows are removed **before** the constraint is added. (ORISO is pre-prod with\nno real users → duplicates can simply be deleted/recreated, not carefully back-filled.)"},"132":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#decision","content":"**Imprint/DPP carry a `draft | published` status.** Counselling may start while the basis\nis still a **draft/unpublished** document; the draft state is **recorded in the audit/log**\n(provisional basis) rather than presented to the client as a finalised legal document."},"133":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#consequences","content":"**Positive:** unambiguous routing (topic → one department → counsellors + imprint/DPP); the\n\"each department its own individualised imprint/DPP\" requirement is satisfied; duplicate-topic\nclass of bug is structurally prevented."},"134":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** a migration is required (dedup existing duplicates, backfill\n`imprint_id`/`dpp_id`, then add the constraint); imprint moves from tenant-only to a\ndepartment-level object (new tables/columns across AgencyService and/or TenantService); admin\nUX change (single-select + dedup tooling); draft/published lifecycle adds state to manage."},"135":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#alternatives-considered","content":"**Support duplicate topics, each with its own imprint** (reject): ambiguous routing — \"topic\n→ which of the duplicate departments?\" has no clean answer; the bug class persists."},"136":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#alternatives-considered","content":"**Keep imprint per-tenant only** (reject): cannot individualise per department, which is the\nwhole legal requirement."},"137":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-01","content":"The DPP half of this decision is already built and live on `dev` (`agency_topic.content_dpp` +\n`publication_status`, `DepartmentDataProtectionService` — commits `54fe868`/`a84e81a`). Confirmed\nin a grill-with-docs session: the remaining work — the `UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)` constraint +\ndedupe migration, and the still-missing per-department Impressum column (the `imprint_id` half) —\nwill be built together in one slice, since both touch `agency_topic`. See also `ADR-009` (Topic\nitself stays global; Department is only where the legal texts live)."},"138":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-03","content":"Verified 2026-07-03: `UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)`, the dedup migration, and the\n`imprint_id`/`dpp_id` reference columns exist ONLY on the stale local branch\n`feat/adr-003-department-agency-topic-unique` in ORISO-AgencyService (base 55 commits behind\n`dev`, pre-AVV; its changeset dir `0021_agency_topic_department` collides with dev's\n`0021_agency_topic_legal` and its SQL lacks `IF NOT EXISTS`). Dev stores DPP inline\n(`agency_topic.content_dpp`), the local branch models references — mutually inconsistent, needs\nrebase + renumber + a reconcile decision (recommend: keep inline `content_dpp`, drop `dpp_id`;\nkeep imprint as a `content_imprint` inline column for symmetry). Per-department imprint not\nstarted anywhere. `AgencyTopicRepository.findByAgency_IdAndTopicId` already assumes uniqueness\n(`Optional` return). Tracked as ORISO-UserService#203 under EPIC #205."},"139":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-07","content":"The 2026-07-03 note above is **superseded** — the reconcile it recommended was carried out and\nthe whole backend now lives on `dev` (the stale reference-column branch was abandoned):"},"140":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-07","content":"**AgencyService (done, on `dev`):** changeset `0023_agency_topic_department` runs the dedup, adds\n`UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)` (guarded by an `onFail=MARK_RAN` precondition), and adds the inline\n`content_imprint` + `publication_status_imprint` columns — mirroring the existing inline\n`content_dpp`/`publication_status` from `0021`. `dpp_id`/`imprint_id` reference columns were\ndropped as recommended. `AgencyTopic` carries all four fields with a `@PrePersist` NOT-NULL guard.\nAdmin API exposes per-department **read + publish** for both DPP and imprint (commit `a2e638f`,\nIDOR-scoped to the caller's agencies). Public, published-only read side is `DepartmentLegalService`\n(draft/never-authored → `null`) wired into `AgencyController`."},"141":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-07","content":"**Admin FE — PR opened:** the agency topic picker becomes **single-select** (was multi-select) —\nthe last open acceptance item of #203. The 2026-06-26 attempt (`02435c3`) was never merged and\n`dev` diverged, so it was re-applied fresh onto current `dev`, then hardened: the id-normalisation\nlogic (previously duplicated across `addAgencyData.ts`, `updateAgencyData.ts`, and the Edit page)\nwas unified into one `normalizeTopicIds()` helper, and test coverage was added where there was\nnone before — `updateAgencyData.ts` had zero tests prior to this PR. See\nORISO-Admin#245\n(`fix/adr-003-agency-single-topic-picker`), not yet merged."},"142":{"id":"/decisions/adr-003-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-003","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-003#implementation-status-2026-07-07","content":"Remaining after this slice: the client-facing render of the department imprint/DPP is part of the\nbroader case-handover client view (#204), not ADR-003 proper."},"143":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"page","content":"ADR-004: Keep the custom chat UI; adopt matrix-js-sdk Megolm under it (don't embed Element Web)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004"},"144":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). June-30 scope and the crypto sequencing are fixed; the SDK-Megolm migration itself is scheduled, not yet built. · Datum: 2026-06-26"},"145":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-11","content":"Implementation amendment — 2026-07-11"},"146":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"Implementation amendment — 2026-07-19 (crypto is now DURABLE, not a disposable proof)"},"147":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#context","content":"Context"},"148":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision-drivers","content":"Decision drivers"},"149":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"Decision"},"150":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"151":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"152":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#sequencing","content":"Sequencing"},"153":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Status & progress (verified 2026-07-10)"},"154":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). June-30 scope and the crypto sequencing are fixed; the SDK-Megolm migration itself is scheduled, not yet built."},"155":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-26"},"156":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product + frontend) + AI (backend)"},"157":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004","content":"**Related:** \\[\\[1 Analysis/ADRS/ADR-005-matrix-federation-off-dns-server-name]] (hard prerequisite — SDK crypto binds device keys to MXIDs), `ORISO-Frontend/CONTEXT.md` (\"labelled-encrypted vs Megolm-encrypted\" flag), findings US-H01 (RC teardown), FE-H11 (1.5s polling), FE-H07 (message-preview leak), US-M04 (queue persistence); `ORISO-Element` (the unused element-web v1.11.55 distribution)"},"158":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-11","content":"`pre-dev` now initializes SDK/Rust crypto before `startClient()` and creates/uses Megolm-encrypted rooms. Real-browser proof covers two users, reload persistence, encrypted advice-seeker membership/messages, and shared two-party Element Calls."},"159":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-11","content":"This is deliberately a **disposable PreDev implementation proof** on the existing bare-IP MXID namespace. It does not revoke ADR-005's durable identity decision. The clean DNS-identity rebuild still precedes real carrier onboarding, and crypto/device/recovery proof must be repeated after it."},"160":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-11","content":"`dev` does not yet contain this implementation; promotion is under review in Frontend #406. Issue #332 is partially delivered by this slice but remains open for key backup/recovery, cross-signing, and durable multi-device verification. Issue #346 remains open because `matrix-js-sdk` is still 38.4."},"161":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"The ADR-005 clean DNS-identity homeserver rebuild is **done**, so the SDK/Rust crypto is no longer the \"disposable PreDev implementation proof\" of the 2026-07-11 amendment — it is the **durable, accepted runtime state**. Verified in `origin/pre-dev` code:"},"162":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"`src/services/matrixClientService.ts` calls `initRustCrypto(...)` **unconditionally** on every client init (IndexedDB store, per-user/device prefix). There is no \"crypto off\" path anymore."},"163":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"Landed beyond what the 07-11 amendment listed as open under #332: key backup (`matrixKeyBackupService.ts`), device isolation / MSC4153 \"invisible crypto\" (`matrixDeviceIsolation.ts`, #438), and the `EncryptionSettings` profile panel."},"164":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"Rooms carry `m.room.encryption` (Helm `MATRIX_ENCRYPTION_ENABLED=true`), so `sendEvent` Megolm-encrypts automatically. Decryption failures are observed live in `utdTracker.ts` via `MatrixEventEvent.Decrypted` / `event.isDecryptionFailure()`."},"165":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"**Superseded as historical** — the following described the pre-crypto state and are no longer true: Context ¶2 (\"matrix-js-sdk crypto is **dormant** … no `initRustCrypto`\"), the Consequences \"no native room encryption\" line, and \"Status & progress (verified 2026-07-10)\" bullet 3 (\"no `initRustCrypto` call on current `origin/dev` or `origin/pre-dev`\"). Residual multi-device-recovery hardening and the `matrix-js-sdk` 38.4 bump may still track under #332/#346; the crypto **activation** decision is fully realised."},"166":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#implementation-amendment--2026-07-19-crypto-is-now-durable-not-a-disposable-proof","content":"The stale in-code comment in `messageSubmitInterfaceComponent.tsx` (\"Matrix messages go through the SDK path unencrypted (ADR-004)\") is corrected in a separate change — its `isEncrypted = false` is the removed **legacy Rocket.Chat** flag, not the Matrix crypto switch."},"167":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#context","content":"The chat is **not** an Element fork. At decision time, `ORISO-Frontend` was the old Caritas/online-beratung Rocket.Chat-based UI with Matrix bolted on alongside. Since Frontend PR #359 and UserService PR #281, the runtime path is Matrix-only; remaining `rc*` names are compatibility wire/database contracts, not an active Rocket.Chat transport. A complete `ORISO-Element` distribution remains an unused reference implementation next to the hand-built frontend."},"168":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#context","content":"The keystone problem remains that **matrix-js-sdk crypto is dormant**: current `origin/dev` and `origin/pre-dev` have no `initRustCrypto()` call, so Olm/Megolm never initializes. PR #359 removed the runtime `crypto-js` dependency and left `useE2EE` as an inert compatibility hook; that removed the old custom encryption path but did **not** add Matrix room encryption. Real Megolm, key backup, cross-signing, and device verification are still missing."},"169":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#context","content":"Constraints shaping the decision: a hard **June 30** feature deadline (live chat \\~90–95% done); a user population with strong **accessibility** needs; and an explicit goal of not reinventing battle-tested logic, while avoiding the \"spend 3 days half-rebuilding, then 10 more days repairing\" trap."},"170":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision-drivers","content":"Full control of UX, theming and **accessibility** (font scaling, contrast, focus, keyboard, screen-reader) for vulnerable users."},"171":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision-drivers","content":"Hit June 30 without a half-finished rebuild reaching the demo."},"172":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision-drivers","content":"Stop reinventing what the SDK gives for free — but adopt it safely, not in the deadline week."},"173":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision-drivers","content":"The chat carries the platform's domain model (agency/Träger, topic, queue/waiting-room, anonymous sessions) that a generic messenger does not."},"174":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"**Keep the hand-built UI as the product surface. Do NOT embed Element Web.** A generic Element timeline does not carry the agency/topic/queue/anonymous model and would cost the accessibility control we want."},"175":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"**Adopt matrix-js-sdk Megolm crypto under the existing UI** (replace the `crypto-js` scheme), but **only after** the clean homeserver rebuild in \\[\\[1 Analysis/ADRS/ADR-005-matrix-federation-off-dns-server-name]] — device keys and key backup bind to MXIDs, and today's MXIDs are built on a bare IP that will change."},"176":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"**Reuse, don't rebuild, where liftable.** Lift ElementCall's settings store, device picker and a11y primitives (font scaling, reduced-motion, keyboard shortcuts) into our shell rather than authoring them."},"177":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"**Use the landed `ChatTransport` facade** as the seam under the custom UI. PR #359 completed the Matrix-only runtime cutover; SDK crypto must be added behind this seam rather than by rebuilding the interface."},"178":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#decision","content":"**Keep transport migration and crypto activation as separate verified steps.** The transport cutover is complete. Crypto activation stays blocked until ADR-005 provides stable DNS-based MXIDs, after which encrypted-room creation and device/key recovery must be proven end to end."},"179":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#considered-options","content":"**Embed Element Web behind the proven ElementCall iframe seam.** Cheapest path to reactions/edits/search/proper crypto (\"days not weeks\" of host-side wrapper). **Rejected** for the product surface: Element is a generic messenger with no agency/topic/queue/anonymous model, and embedding forfeits the accessibility control that motivates the whole effort. Kept on the table only as a possible future spike, not the chosen direction."},"180":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#considered-options","content":"**Keep the custom UI and keep crypto-js indefinitely.** No crypto migration. &#x2A;*Rejected:** leaves us permanently reinventing pagination/reactions/edits/search and without key backup or device verification, and keeps the \"labelled-but-not-encrypted\" hazard."},"181":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#considered-options","content":"**Adopt SDK Megolm now (in the deadline week).** &#x2A;*Rejected:** blocked by the bare-IP `server_name` (ADR-005); enabling crypto first means redoing it after the homeserver rebuild, and touching crypto under deadline pressure risks a plaintext leak."},"182":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#consequences","content":"**Positive:** full UX/accessibility control; the Matrix-vs-RC branch collapses once the facade lands, so Rocket.Chat becomes deletable; over time the SDK delivers pagination/reactions/edits/redactions/read-receipts/key-backup for \"free\"; the June-30 path cannot half-break the demo (strangler flag)."},"183":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** we keep maintaining the timeline shell ourselves; the SDK-Megolm migration is a real project that touches login, room creation, device identity, backup, and recovery and **must** be sequenced after ADR-005. Until then the Matrix-only runtime has no native room encryption."},"184":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#sequencing","content":"**Completed:** Matrix-only runtime cutover via Frontend #359 and UserService #281; old custom crypto removed from the runtime; remaining `rc*` names are coordinated-contract cleanup."},"185":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#sequencing","content":"**Next, after ADR-005:** upgrade/adapt the SDK as needed, call `initRustCrypto`, create truly encrypted rooms, add key backup/cross-signing/device verification, and prove multi-user/multi-device recovery before dependent group-E2EE features."},"186":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend #359 merged 2026-07-04: Matrix-only `ChatTransport`, Matrix receipts/timeline, Rocket.Chat frontend/runtime removal, inert `useE2EE` compatibility API, no SDK crypto."},"187":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"UserService #281 merged 2026-07-03: `rocket-chat.enabled=false` by default and Matrix-only group/session provisioning; legacy DB/DTO names remain."},"188":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend #332 and #346 are open. `matrix-js-sdk` is still 38.4 and there is no `initRustCrypto` call on current `origin/dev` or `origin/pre-dev`."},"189":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"ADR-005 is only partially applied. Federation hardening reached Pre-Dev, but the homeserver still uses the bare-IP `server_name`; the clean rebuild remains the hard blocker."},"190":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"ORISO-Helm PR #32 and UserService PR #370 were opened on 2026-07-09 and are green. They lock configurable DNS-based Matrix identity and MXID invariants, but they do not provide the required Pre-Dev `matrix.oriso-dev.site` overlay, perform the clean DNS/TLS-backed homeserver install, or initialize crypto."},"191":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend PR #389 was closed without merge. Its removal of encrypted-room guards and `matrixRoomEncryption` is the opposite of this accepted ADR and must not be reused. The current `pre-dev` code still retains the encryption helper."},"192":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend PR #397 targets `pre-dev` and changes Matrix client construction for logging. The Megolm implementation must preserve its logger injection or resolve that small overlap after it lands; it must not duplicate the logging work."},"193":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"The former `feat/chat-transport-facade` worktree note below is historical. Its\nbehavior was subsumed by merged PR #359; it is not an active implementation\nbranch. New crypto work uses isolated worktrees from `origin/pre-dev` and never\nuses `main`."},"194":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-50","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**Historical first slice (later subsumed by merged PR #359):**"},"195":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-51","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**#303 — `ChatTransport` seam DONE.** New `src/services/chatTransport/`:\n`ChatTransport` interface + `MatrixChatTransport` adapter (pure delegation to\n`MatrixClientService`) + `getChatTransport()` bound to the client registry,\nwith 8 contract tests. Nothing routes through it yet (that is #304)."},"196":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-52","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**#307 — ci-main now gates on `npm run test:unit`** (previously build-only) and\nfour dead call-widget duplicates removed."},"197":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-53","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**#306 — FE-H07 regression test added.** The leak is already closed on `dev`\n(`apiSendMessage` forwards no `messagePreview` on the Matrix path); the test\nlocks that boundary so the twice-seen re-leak now fails CI."},"198":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-54","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**Survey corrections to the original sequencing (2026-06-28):**"},"199":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-55","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**FE-M08 is already on `dev`** (`src/utils/matrixRoomUtils.ts` centralises\n`isMatrixRoom`) — no work needed; the original plan over-counted it."},"200":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-56","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**Component re-routing (#304) and the polling fix (#305) are HELD.** Open PRs\n\\#126 (focus-ring) and #275 (case-handover) edit\n`matrixClientService`/`messageSubmitInterfaceComponent`/`SessionStream`; routing\nthrough them now would collide. Build after they merge, then rebase."},"201":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-57","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"**The in-flight modernization has landed: react-router v5→v7 (PR #329 MERGED)**\non top of React 19.2.3. The chat branch (based on pre-v7 `dev`, now \\~30 commits\nbehind) must be **rebased onto current `dev` and re-tested under router v7**\nbefore it is pushed — this is the \"re-test against the modernization\" step."},"202":{"id":"/decisions/adr-004-58","page_id":"/decisions/adr-004","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-004#status--progress-verified-2026-07-10","content":"Net: the keystone seam exists and is safe; the risky component surgery is\ndeliberately deferred behind the collision holds + the router-v7 rebase."},"203":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"page","content":"ADR-005: Matrix federation deliberately OFF; real DNS server_name via a clean homeserver rebuild","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005"},"204":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). Timing fixed: the clean rebuild runs early July, before any SDK-crypto work and before real carrier onboarding. · Datum: 2026-06-26"},"205":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"PreDev implementation exception — 2026-07-11"},"206":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"Context"},"207":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision-drivers","content":"Decision drivers"},"208":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"Decision"},"209":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"210":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"211":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"Status & progress (updated 2026-07-02)"},"212":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). Timing fixed: the clean rebuild runs early July, before any SDK-crypto work and before real carrier onboarding."},"213":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-26"},"214":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + neusta (ops own the homeserver/SSH access)"},"215":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005","content":"**Related:** \\[\\[1 Analysis/ADRS/ADR-004-chat-keep-custom-ui-adopt-matrix-sdk-megolm]] (SDK-Megolm adoption depends on stable MXIDs), findings K8-M09 / K8-M06 (insecure key handling) / DB-H04 / DB-M09 (bare-IP server\\_name baked into MXIDs)"},"216":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"The sequencing rule is amended for disposable PreDev validation only:"},"217":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"SDK/Rust Megolm may run on the current legacy bare-IP namespace to prove application behavior before the ops-owned rebuild."},"218":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"All accounts, rooms, devices, and crypto stores created under that namespace are disposable and must not become the durable onboarding identity."},"219":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"The clean `matrix.oriso-dev.site` rebuild with federation off remains mandatory before real carrier onboarding."},"220":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"After the rebuild, repeat multi-user messaging, reload, multi-device/recovery, audio, and video proof."},"221":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#predev-implementation-exception--2026-07-11","content":"This exception records observed reality; it does not make `server_name` mutable or accept the bare-IP namespace as the final architecture. Helm #31 tracks the rebuild. Helm PR #32 was closed without merge; UserService PR #370 remains open."},"222":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"Matrix federation in ORISO is currently &#x2A;*misconfigured, not deliberately off — the worst of both worlds.** Synapse runs federation **on by default**: the homeserver listener resources include `federation`, there is no `federation_domain_whitelist` / `send_federation: false` anywhere, a federation port (8009/8448) is exposed, and a `.well-known/matrix/server` delegation is advertised. At the same time it is broken and weakened:"},"223":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"**`server_name` is a bare IP** (`91.99.219.182`, earlier `91.99.183.160`). This is the known anti-pattern: it bakes the IP into **every** MXID (`@user:91.99.219.182`), so any IP change orphans all users and rooms, and it cannot federate properly."},"224":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"`accept_keys_insecurely: true` and `suppress_key_validation_warnings: true` actively weaken the federation that is left on."},"225":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"The only \"off\" switch present is cosmetic and client-side (`ORISO-Element/config.json` `disable_federation: true`), with a domain that doesn't even match."},"226":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#context","content":"`server_name` is **immutable after the homeserver's first start** and is already embedded in MXIDs, so this cannot be fixed in place. There are **no production users** today."},"227":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision-drivers","content":"ORISO is a **closed counselling platform on a single homeserver**; there is no use case for federating with the open Matrix network, and federation only enlarges the attack surface."},"228":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision-drivers","content":"**MXID stability is a hard prerequisite** for adopting matrix-js-sdk Megolm crypto (\\[\\[1 Analysis/ADRS/ADR-004-chat-keep-custom-ui-adopt-matrix-sdk-megolm]]): device keys and key backup bind to MXIDs, so the `server_name` must be final before crypto is enabled."},"229":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision-drivers","content":"No production users → no migration cost; delete + recreate is acceptable (consistent with the project's \"pre-prod, skip migration\" rule)."},"230":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"Do a **clean homeserver rebuild** with:"},"231":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"environment-specific stable Matrix identity names, never a bare IP:"},"232":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"Pre-Dev: `server_name = matrix.oriso-dev.site`;"},"233":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"Dev: `server_name = matrix.oriso.org`;"},"234":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"Production/Main is outside the authorized scope of this work;"},"235":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"federation **explicitly off** — `federation_domain_whitelist: []` (or `send_federation: false`), and drop the federation listener / port 8009/8448 and the `.well-known/matrix/server` delegation;"},"236":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"remove `accept_keys_insecurely` and `suppress_key_validation_warnings`."},"237":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"**Timing:** early July — **after** June 30 (the rebuild is *not* a prerequisite for the June-30 features, which run on the current homeserver) and **before** any SDK-crypto work and before onboarding real carriers. No data migration: existing test accounts/rooms are discarded and recreated."},"238":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#decision","content":"**Ownership:** neusta/ops own the homeserver and SSH/kubectl access; the AI cannot and will not perform the rebuild (it is unowned infra). The AI prepares config and verification steps only."},"239":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#considered-options","content":"**Leave the bare-IP, half-on configuration.** &#x2A;*Rejected:** every additional account gets a broken `@user:IP` identity, federation stays on-yet-weakened, and SDK-crypto adoption stays blocked. The cleanup debt grows daily."},"240":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#considered-options","content":"**Keep federation ON, but do it properly** (real DNS, key validation, a whitelist). &#x2A;*Rejected:** there is no counselling use case for federation; it is pure added attack surface and operational complexity."},"241":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#considered-options","content":"**Fix `server_name` in place without a rebuild.** &#x2A;*Impossible:** `server_name` is immutable after first start and is already in every MXID."},"242":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#consequences","content":"**Positive:** stable, DNS-based MXIDs that survive IP changes; a smaller attack surface appropriate for a counselling tool; unblocks the SDK-Megolm crypto adoption in ADR-004; resolves DB-H04 / K8-M09 / K8-M06 in one move."},"243":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** requires a clean rebuild and ops bandwidth (neusta); all current test accounts/rooms are discarded; it must happen **before** crypto adoption or that work is redone. The dependency makes ADR-004 step 2 (SDK Megolm) wait on this."},"244":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"**Environment mapping clarified 2026-07-10:** Pre-Dev is the runtime source of\ntruth for this initiative and must use `matrix.oriso-dev.site`. The separate\nDev environment may use `matrix.oriso.org`. ORISO-Helm PR #32 (base `dev`)\nmakes the value configurable and adds red-green guard tests against bare-IP\nidentity config, but its `matrix.oriso.org` default must not be mistaken for\nthe Pre-Dev overlay. The PR is green and open; the Pre-Dev value, DNS/TLS, and\nthe clean live install remain pending."},"245":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"**Partially executed on Pre-Dev (oriso-dev.site) 2026-07-02** as part of the\nfull-Matrix migration: Synapse upgraded **1.153.0 → v1.155.0** (latest stable,\npinned tag instead of `:latest`), **federation listener resource removed**\n(`/_matrix/federation` now 404), `federation_domain_whitelist: []` set, and\n`accept_keys_insecurely` / `suppress_key_validation_warnings` **removed** —\napplied via `kubectl` on the pre-dev node (same mechanism as the sanctioned\nUserService hot-deploy). Backups: configmap + SQLite online backup\n(`/data/homeserver.db.bak-20260702-pre1155`), local copies in\n`~/ORISO/_e2e-artifacts/matrix-upgrade-20260702/`. &#x2A;*Note:** the deployment is\nhelm-managed (`oriso-platform-matrix-synapse`), so a future `helm upgrade` from\nORISO-Kubernetes will revert the image/config unless the chart is updated —\nthat chart update belongs to the neusta rebuild."},"246":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"**`server_name` deliberately NOT touched** — still the bare IP\n`91.99.183.160`. Changing it requires the clean rebuild (wipes MXIDs), which\nstays **owned by neusta/ops**. No AI action on that part: the homeserver\nrebuild itself is unowned infra."},"247":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"The June-30 frontend work (\\[\\[1 Analysis/ADRS/ADR-004-chat-keep-custom-ui-adopt-matrix-sdk-megolm]])\nruns on the current bare-IP homeserver and does **not** touch crypto, so it is\nnot blocked by this rebuild. The unrelated react-router v7 migration landing on\n`dev` (PR #329) has no bearing here."},"248":{"id":"/decisions/adr-005-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-005","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-005#status--progress-updated-2026-07-02","content":"**Action for Frank/neusta:** provision DNS/TLS for `matrix.oriso-dev.site` on\nPre-Dev (and `matrix.oriso.org` separately on Dev), then do\nthe clean rebuild (federation off, drop the federation listener/`.well-known`,\nremove `accept_keys_insecurely`). This is the first hard prerequisite for the\nJuly crypto step and must precede `initRustCrypto`."},"249":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"page","content":"ADR-006: `conversation_type` as a persisted modality field, rolled out selector-first","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006"},"250":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session). Decision made; implementation scheduled. · Datum: 2026-06-28"},"251":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"Superseding rollout note — 2026-07-11"},"252":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#context","content":"Context"},"253":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"Decision"},"254":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"255":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"256":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Rollout runbook (for the hardening devs)"},"257":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-006#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"Status & progress (2026-06-30)"},"258":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session). Decision made; implementation scheduled."},"259":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-28"},"260":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product + frontend) + AI (backend)"},"261":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006","content":"**Related:** `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md` (the glossary this enforces), `ADR-001-counselling-modalities-as-modules.md` (registration-side view of the same axes), the chat-transport work (`ADR-004`/`ADR-005`), memories `oriso-dev-cluster-liquibase-disabled-configmap`, `oriso-tenantservice-liquibase-disabled`, `oriso-predev-deploy-and-ci-model`. `ADR-009` (2026-07-01) adds admin-editable/translatable **display labels** for the four values below — the enum and its per-value code paths are unchanged, not reopened by that decision."},"262":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"Frontend PR #340 merged the `getModality()` selector, but production components still do not use it; the selector call-site sweep remains open in Frontend #409."},"263":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"UserService does not yet persist `conversation_type`; UserService #382 owns the enum, Liquibase migration/backfill, creation-path stamping, and DTO projection."},"264":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"The Liquibase-off premise below is historical. On current PreDev, all four backend deployments expose `SPRING_LIQUIBASE_ENABLED=true`; UserService, TenantService, and AgencyService log clean changelog runs. ADR-006 therefore uses a registered boot-time UserService changeset, not a manual per-environment `ALTER`."},"265":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"Preserve the safety invariant behind the old wording: schema migration must complete before Hibernate validates the new entity fields. PreDev must prove the new changeset ran and the pod became ready."},"266":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#superseding-rollout-note--2026-07-11","content":"Frontend #410 is the current epic; #408 is the four-modality real-browser gate. Reachable Email is outside this ADR."},"267":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#context","content":"The platform has four conversation **modalities** — Agency Counselling, Live Chat, Internal Group Chat, Self-Help Group — but **no field anywhere stores which one a conversation is**. The kind is re-derived from scattered booleans (`registrationType`, `postcode`, `Anonymous-` username prefix, `teamSession`, `repetitive`, `consultant`-mismatch, presence of `matrixRoomId`) at \\~90 frontend call sites and in backend queries. This is the verified root cause of the recurring \"every time we touch the live chat, the chat goes fuzzy\" failures: modality, lifecycle status, and structural shape are conflated (e.g. `getSessionType()` returns `enquiry | archived | group | session`, mixing three axes), so a change in one bleeds into the others."},"268":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#context","content":"Verification (5-agent workflow, 2026-06-28) established two facts that shape the decision:"},"269":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#context","content":"**The entity split is not clean.** Agency Counselling and Live Chat are `Session` rows; Self-Help is a `Chat` row; **Internal Group Chat is dual-stored** — `createSimplifiedGroupChat` writes both a `Session` (`teamSession=true`, `registrationType=REGISTERED`) and a `Chat` row, and its `Session` shape differs from Agency Counselling **only by the `teamSession` flag**. So `teamSession` must be evaluated before `registrationType`, and the new column must exist on **both** `session` and `chat`."},"270":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#context","content":"**The naive \"just add the column\" path is the signature ORISO crash, and worse than a 500.** The dev cluster's `oriso-userservice-config` ConfigMap forces `SPRING_LIQUIBASE_ENABLED=false`, overriding the image's `application-dev.properties`; `spring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=validate` is active in every environment. A mapped `@Column` with no matching DB column fails at `SessionFactory` initialisation → **pod CrashLoopBackOff at boot** (the whole UserService won't start), not a per-request error. The same holds for pre-dev/staging/prod (validate + Liquibase off everywhere)."},"271":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Introduce an explicit `conversationType` modality** as the single source of truth, values `AGENCY_COUNSELLING · LIVE_CHAT · INTERNAL_GROUP · SELF_HELP`. &#x2A;*Modality (what kind) and lifecycle status (what stage) are two separate fields and must never be merged into one \"type\" again.**"},"272":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Persist it** as a nullable `conversation_type` column on both `session` and `chat` (backend is the eventual source of truth), but **roll it out selector-first** so the field can land without a half-migration crash:"},"273":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Step 1 — frontend read-contract first.** A single pure selector `getModality(conversation): Modality` becomes the *only* place modality is decided. It prefers `dto.conversationType` when present and **falls back** to the existing heuristic when null. The \\~90 call sites collapse to this one function immediately — risk-free, no backend dependency, unit-tested with vitest. Fallback order (verified): `chat` present → (`repetitive`+WEEKLY ? `SELF_HELP` : `INTERNAL_GROUP`); else `teamSession` → `INTERNAL_GROUP`; else `registrationType===ANONYMOUS` → `LIVE_CHAT`; else `AGENCY_COUNSELLING`."},"274":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Step 2 — the column, Liquibase-before-Hibernate.** Add nullable `@Column` mappings plus one registered UserService changeset for `session` and `chat`, with deterministic legacy backfill and idempotent preconditions. Boot-time Liquibase is now the schema source of truth; verify its execution before accepting Hibernate readiness. Manual ALTER is emergency fallback only, not the normal rollout."},"275":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Step 3 — stamp at creation.** Default `conversationType` at the two choke-points `SessionService.saveSession` and `ChatService.saveChat`, plus explicit stamping in `createSimplifiedGroupChat` (both rows), `AnonymousConversationCreatorService` (`LIVE_CHAT`), and the easy-to-miss `AskerImportService` and `ChatReCreator` (carry-forward) paths."},"276":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#decision","content":"**Backfill is trivial and disposable.** With no production users, existing rows get a one-time `UPDATE` from the heuristic, or are wiped and recreated. The heuristic in `getModality()` stays only as a null-fallback and is deleted once the column is confirmed populated everywhere."},"277":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#considered-options","content":"**Direct backend field, deploy immediately (Frank's first instinct).** Cleanest end state, no \"two truths\" window. &#x2A;*Rejected as the *sequence*, kept as the *target*:** deploying a mapped column before the DB has it = CrashLoopBackOff given validate + Liquibase-off. The selector-first sequence reaches the same end state safely."},"278":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#considered-options","content":"**Frontend-derived selector only, no column ever.** Cheapest, no migration. &#x2A;*Rejected:** leaves the source of truth as a heuristic forever; backend queries (e.g. the live-chat queue) still can't filter cleanly by modality, and the `postcode='00000'` conflation recurs server-side."},"279":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#considered-options","content":"**Keep deriving per call site.** &#x2A;*Rejected:** this is the status quo that produces the recurring fuzziness."},"280":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#consequences","content":"**Positive:** one source of truth for modality; the \\~90 heuristic sites collapse to one tested function on day one; modality and status stop colliding; new modalities (Self-Help, future video) become an additive enum value; the live-chat queue can filter by `conversation_type` instead of `postcode='00000'`."},"281":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** current live Liquibase activation still drifts from the unfinished Helm defaults (#10/#11), so migration logs and permissions must be checked during rollout; `INTERNAL_GROUP` must be stamped on two rows; ambiguous historical `SELF_HELP` rows must remain nullable or be explicitly audited rather than guessed."},"282":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Merge `getModality()` selector + vitest; confirm the \\~90 sites read only the selector."},"283":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Add nullable `@Column` mappings + registered changeset/backfill and test an empty/current MariaDB schema locally."},"284":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Merge to `pre-dev`; deploy the regular image and verify Liquibase executes the new changeset before Hibernate validation and health becomes green."},"285":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Verify Agency Counselling, Live Chat, Internal Group, and Self-Help creation end to end on PreDev."},"286":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#rollout-runbook-for-the-hardening-devs","content":"Confirm no `NULL` `conversation_type` after creating one of each modality; then drop the heuristic fallback."},"287":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"**Step 1 built locally (additive, green):** a pure `getModality(item): Modality` selector + `Modality` enum (`AGENCY_COUNSELLING · LIVE_CHAT · INTERNAL_GROUP · SELF_HELP`) in `src/components/session/getModality.ts`, with the verified fallback order and an explicit-`conversationType`-wins path, 8 vitest cases (red→green), `tsc --noEmit` clean. Worktree `feature/adr006-getmodality-selector` off `origin/dev`, **not pushed**."},"288":{"id":"/decisions/adr-006-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-006","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-006#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"The \\~90-site sweep (routing existing call sites through the selector) is **intentionally deferred** — it collides with open PRs #126/#275 on the hot files. Only the selector + tests landed; Steps 2–3 (the `conversation_type` column, manual ALTER-before-deploy) remain backend work for the post-collision window."},"289":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"page","content":"ADR-007: Live-chat liveness — the indicator reads backend Availability, never mirrors or infers it","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007"},"290":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session). Root causes verified; fix scheduled. · Datum: 2026-06-28"},"291":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"Context"},"292":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"Decision"},"293":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#considered-options-badge-gating","content":"Considered options (badge gating)"},"294":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"295":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"Resolved product questions (Frank, 2026-06-28)"},"296":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-007#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"Status & progress (2026-06-30)"},"297":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session). Root causes verified; fix scheduled."},"298":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-28"},"299":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"300":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007","content":"**Related:** `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md` (Availability / Waiting room terms), `ADR-005-matrix-federation-off-dns-server-name` (the badge-gating trade-off touches this), `ADR-006` (the modality field). Findings from the 2026-06-28 liveness verification workflow."},"301":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"The recurring complaint \"the live chat keeps showing people as *live* when nobody is\" is **not** an architecture gap, contrary to a first reading. Verification established that the backend **Availability** model is sound and already implements exactly the product intent (an explicit \"go live\" toggle, auto-off on logout, TTL-bounded):"},"302":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"`ConsultantActivityRegistry` (in-memory) holds the currently-available counsellors; `CONSULTANT_AVAILABILITY_ACTIVE_WINDOW_MS = 120000` (120s TTL); `ConsultantActivityInterceptor.refreshIfAvailable` heartbeats on every authenticated counsellor request; logout calls `apiSetLiveChatAvailability(false)`."},"303":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"This is **deliberately decoupled from Matrix/RC presence**, because Matrix presence is unreliable for live chat (noted in `TopicConsultantRoutingService`)."},"304":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"The bug is that the **visible** liveness has **three independent wrong sources**, none of which read that authoritative model:"},"305":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"**Nav green pill** — driven entirely by a `localStorage` flag (`caritas_liveChatAvailability`, `liveChatToggle.ts`), a *write-only mirror* that re-asserts FE→BE but never reads BE→FE. When the 120s TTL drops the counsellor, the pill stays lit indefinitely (`NavigationBar.tsx`)."},"306":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"**Per-session \"live\" badge** — derived from chat **type** (`isAnonymousChat ? 'live' : 'nearby'`, `SessionHeaderComponent.tsx:742`), so *every* Live Chat session shows \"live\" regardless of presence."},"307":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"**Persisted `Session.status = ACTIVE`** — never reset when a live chat is abandoned; the reaper (`DeactivateAnonymousUserService`) only sweeps after a 6h window (`deactivateworkflow.periodMinutes=360`), so a dead session reads live for hours."},"308":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#context","content":"Separately, the Live-Chat queue uses `ORDER BY s.createDate DESC` in three `SessionRepository` queries (lines 211/229/248) — newest-first — while the ratsuchende's \"people ahead of me\" position counts oldest-first, so list order and position disagree (a FIFO bug)."},"309":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"**Availability stays backend-authoritative; the indicator becomes a READ of it, never a mirror.** Add `GET /conversations/consultants/availability` (self) returning `{available}` from `ConsultantActivityRegistry.filterActive()`; the nav polls it (interval \\< 120s TTL, e.g. 30–45s) and drives the pill from the result. Make the `localStorage` store TTL-aware (expiry stamp; treat as OFF on an unavailable/empty poll). The FE→BE re-assert must not silently re-mark a counsellor available without intent."},"310":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"**The per-session badge stops keying on chat type.** Gate \"live\" on Availability / active-session state (and never show \"live\" for `DONE`), **not** on `isAnonymousChat`."},"311":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"**Abandoned live sessions get a prompt, live-chat-specific teardown** — transition the owned `IN_PROGRESS` session to `DONE` on counsellor logout/toggle-off (reuse `DeactivateSessionActionCommand`), and apply a live-chat-specific timeout in minutes, separate from the 6h anonymous-user deactivation window."},"312":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"**Queue is true FIFO** — change the three `ORDER BY createDate DESC` to `ASC` so list order matches the position count."},"313":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#decision","content":"**Keep the waiting room decoupled** — the ratsuchende continues to see only FIFO position, never counsellor Availability (see CONTEXT). None of this needs a schema change, so it does not touch the Liquibase-off hazard."},"314":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#considered-options-badge-gating","content":"**Gate the per-session badge on real-time RC/Matrix presence.** Most \"honest\", but couples the fix to the unreliable presence layer and the ADR-005 Matrix rebuild. &#x2A;*Rejected for now.**"},"315":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#considered-options-badge-gating","content":"**Gate it on Availability / active-session state (chosen).** Transport-agnostic, ships immediately, consistent with the deliberate decoupling from Matrix/RC presence."},"316":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#consequences","content":"**Positive:** the green pill and per-session badge finally reflect reality; the whole fix ships now, independent of the Matrix SDK rebuild; FIFO order and position agree. &#x2A;*Negative / cost:** a poll adds light traffic (bounded by the TTL); on a backend restart the in-memory registry empties, so all counsellors read unavailable until they re-toggle — which is the *correct* behaviour and must not be \"fixed\" by auto-re-asserting from the stale FE flag."},"317":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"**Time-to-DONE** for an abandoned `IN_PROGRESS` live session → **10 minutes** (a live-chat-specific window, separate from the 6h anonymous-user deactivation sweep)."},"318":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"**Idle-but-toggled-on*&#x2A; → keep the existing **\\~2.5h inactivity auto-logout**; the per-request heartbeat keeps an actively-working counsellor available, so the availability poll should not flip a working counsellor OFF on its own. **New feature spun off** (separate task / mini-spec): a **pre-logout warning \\~5 min before** auto-logout, delivered as a notification (optionally with a distinct \"logged-out\" sound), offering **extend** buttons (+1h / +3h / max 6h). To be located in the existing auto-logout code, then built or at minimum documented."},"319":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"**Badge gating** → &#x2A;*option (b)**: gate the per-session \"live\" badge on Availability / active-session state, not real RC/Matrix presence — keeps the whole fix transport-agnostic and independent of ADR-005."},"320":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"**After a backend restart** → **force counsellors to re-toggle**; do not auto-re-assert availability from the stale FE flag (that resurrects stuck-live)."},"321":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#resolved-product-questions-frank-2026-06-28","content":"> The exact auto-logout mechanism (≈2.5h) is being located in code so the warning/extend feature attaches to the real implementation."},"322":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"**Slice 1 of 4 built locally (additive, green):** the self-availability READ — `GET /conversations/consultants/availability` returning `{available}` from `ConsultantActivityRegistry.filterActive()` — is implemented on the existing `ConsultantLiveAvailabilityController` (**no SecurityConfig change** — the `/conversations/consultants/**` rule already covers the GET) with a 3-case `WebMvcTest` (active / inactive / non-consultant), red→green. Worktree `feature/adr007-consultant-availability-read` off `origin/dev`, **not pushed**."},"323":{"id":"/decisions/adr-007-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-007","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-007#status--progress-2026-06-30","content":"**Held (collide with open PRs, queued):** the per-session badge gating (`SessionHeaderComponent` — collision-safe, next up), the nav-pill read (`NavigationBar` — HOLD behind #126), and the FIFO `ASC` + 10-min live-chat teardown (`SessionRepository` — HOLD behind case-handover #186). Build after those merge / rebase."},"324":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"page","content":"ADR-008: Supervision — keep per-session agency-scoped reach; move side-channels out of the client's room","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008"},"325":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008","content":"Status: Proposed — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session); U25 cohort + go-live date resolved 2026-06-30 (minors are in U25 scope; go-live 2026-10-01, no 30.06 launch). The separate-room side-channel exclusion is therefore a confirmed pre-go-live blocker (with runway). Still pending: the data-protection officer's exact disclosure wording and the add-supervisor authority/consent details. · Datum: 2026-06-28"},"326":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#context","content":"Context"},"327":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#decision-proposed","content":"Decision (proposed)"},"328":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"Considered options (hiding the side-channel)"},"329":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"330":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#open-pending-franks-final-requirements--data-protection-officer","content":"Open (pending Frank's final requirements + data-protection officer)"},"331":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"Addendum 2026-07-13 (grill-with-docs): standing auto-assignment + unified opt-out consent"},"332":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008","content":"**Status:** Proposed — 2026-06-28 (grill-with-docs session); U25 cohort + go-live date **resolved 2026-06-30** (minors **are** in U25 scope; go-live **2026-10-01**, no 30.06 launch). The separate-room side-channel exclusion is therefore a **confirmed pre-go-live blocker** (with runway). Still pending: the data-protection officer's exact disclosure wording and the add-supervisor authority/consent details."},"333":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008","content":"**Date:** 2026-06-28"},"334":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering); data-protection officer (open)"},"335":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008","content":"**Related:** `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md` (Supervision, Peer, Coordinator, Selective in-room visibility), `ADR-002-silent-room-membership-and-access-control-curtain` (same \"is it actually enforced?\" class), `ADR-004`/`ADR-005` (Megolm is now on and durable post-rebuild — but it does NOT provide in-room confidentiality here: room members decrypt every event, see below), memory `oriso-case-handover-cho-01` (reason+consent+audit pattern), `oriso-agency-admin-cross-traeger-leak` (the unscoped-access leak class). Driver: **U25** suicide counselling with **Peers** coordinated by **Coordinators**."},"336":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#context","content":"Verification (2026-06-28) corrected two assumptions:"},"337":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#context","content":"**Supervision reach is well-built, not an unbounded global IDOR.** There are two distinct things: (A) a cosmetic frontend flag `isSupervisorView = consultant.id !== userData.userId` (UI only); and (B) the *real* feature — a `SessionSupervisor` entity + **real Matrix membership**. `addSupervisor` (`SessionSupervisorFacade`) genuinely `inviteUserToRoom` + `setUserPowerLevel(10, read-only observer)` + `joinRoom`; read paths are gated by `isSupervisor(consultant, session)` = `findBySessionIdAndSupervisorConsultantIdAndIsActiveTrue`. So a supervisor reaches **exactly the sessions explicitly assigned to them**, and the add-gate is **agency-scoped** — *not* cross-Träger, *not* all-cases. The \"built globally\" impression is the cosmetic flag (A); the real reach (B) is per-session and agency-bounded."},"338":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#context","content":"**The real risk is the side-channel direction, and it is HIGH for U25 minors.** A supervisor legitimately *reading* the client room is intended. The breach is the reverse: the supervisor's feedback (`[SUPERVISOR_FEEDBACK]` prefix) **and** the coordinator↔peer asides (`[VISIBLE_TO:uid…]` prefix) are posted into the **same room as the minor** and hidden **only** by a React `return null` (`MessageItemComponent.tsx`). The Matrix retrieval path filters nothing (`getRoomMessages` streams every event); Megolm is now on but does not help here — the minor is a legitimate room member and decrypts every event; there is no server ACL — so the full plaintext aside is **delivered to the minor's own client** and is trivially recoverable (DevTools, network tab, any non-ORISO Matrix client). For a suicidal minor, an exposed clinical aside or supervisor critique is a safeguarding hazard, not a cosmetic bug. This is the concrete form of the \"Matrix isn't deep enough = technical debt\" question."},"339":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#context","content":"A second, lesser risk (AXIS 2): the `addSupervisor` authority gate is \"assigned consultant **or** same agency,\" so any same-agency consultant can attach any `is_supervisor` colleague to any in-progress case, silently to the minor (notification, no veto), with only a free-text note."},"340":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#decision-proposed","content":"**Keep reach per-session-explicit and agency-scoped.** Do **not** widen supervision to cross-agency/cross-Träger \"global\" oversight; that re-opens the unscoped-access leak class ORISO already suffered. If cross-agency oversight is a genuine U25 requirement, it must get an explicit tenant-aware design, not a relaxed `areFromSameAgency` check."},"341":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#decision-proposed","content":"**Stop relying on in-room prefixes for confidentiality. Move all side-channels to a separate room.** Supervisor↔counsellor feedback and coordinator↔peer asides live in a **separate Matrix room the client is never invited to**. The supervisor still joins the client room read-only for observation; only their *feedback* moves out. This is **transport-agnostic** — it does **not** wait for the Megolm/homeserver rebuild (ADR-005)."},"342":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#decision-proposed","content":"**Treat `[VISIBLE_TO:]`/`[SUPERVISOR_FEEDBACK]` visual hiding as non-confidential.** It may remain as a UX affordance only where every room member is *allowed* to see the content; it must never be the boundary protecting a minor from a clinical aside."},"343":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#decision-proposed","content":"**Tighten add-supervisor authority + record consent/justification**, mirroring the Case-Handover (CAR-CHO-01) reason+consent+audit pattern: restrict who may attach a supervisor, require a recorded justification, and disclose supervision to the ratsuchende (via the agency's privacy policy + Impressum on chat entry). Exact disclosure wording is pending the data-protection officer; the disclose-vs-conceal toggle is trivial to add."},"344":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"**In-room prefix + frontend `return null` (current).** Rejected as confidentiality — the data still reaches the minor's device."},"345":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"**Separate Matrix room for asides (chosen).** Real exclusion, transport-agnostic, ships now. Cost: more rooms to provision + UI thread/context-linking."},"346":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"**Megolm per-recipient subset (one room, cryptographic).** The only way to keep a single room *and* hide asides, but blocked on Megolm being off (ADR-004/005) — deferred, not the launch answer."},"347":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"**Server-side filtering in `getRoomMessages`.** Defence-in-depth only; a client hitting Synapse `/sync` directly (E2EE off) still gets everything. Not sufficient alone."},"348":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#considered-options-hiding-the-side-channel","content":"**Matrix power levels / ACL.** Govern who may *send*, not who may *read* existing events — does not hide content within a shared room."},"349":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#consequences","content":"**Positive:** the U25 safeguarding leak is closed with a transport-agnostic change (no waiting for the crypto rebuild); supervision reach stays safely bounded; authority/consent gains an auditable trail. &#x2A;*Negative / cost:** the side-channel becomes a real separate room to manage and link in the UI; \"one room with cryptographically hidden asides\" remains a future (post-Megolm) nicety, not the near-term shape."},"350":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#open-pending-franks-final-requirements--data-protection-officer","content":"~~Is visual-only hiding acceptable as an interim before U25 onboards real minors, or is the separate-room exclusion a hard pre-launch blocker?~~ &#x2A;*Resolved (Frank, 2026-06-30):** there is **no 30.06 go-live**; go-live is **2026-10-01** and **U25 will include real minors**. The separate-room exclusion is a **hard pre-go-live blocker** (must land before 2026-10-01), not an acceptable interim — but it has runway (the late-June two weeks are build time, not a launch). It stays transport-agnostic, so it does **not** wait on the ADR-005 homeserver rebuild; build it within the runway."},"351":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#open-pending-franks-final-requirements--data-protection-officer","content":"~~Who may attach a supervisor, and must the ratsuchende/guardian consent or be able to veto?~~ &#x2A;*Resolved twice, see below:** authority resolved 2026-07-04 (US#302); consent/veto resolved 2026-07-13 (this addendum)."},"352":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#open-pending-franks-final-requirements--data-protection-officer","content":"Is cross-agency/cross-Träger supervision a real requirement, or is agency-scoped (current) correct?"},"353":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#open-pending-franks-final-requirements--data-protection-officer","content":"Audit/retention: is the `SessionSupervisor` addedDate/removedDate row sufficient, or is a richer \"who supervised which minor's case when\" record required?"},"354":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"Prompted by a Shazia bug report about Supervision \"bleeding into\" Case Handover. Investigation found no regression — the side-room fix from this ADR (shipped as US#293/FE#367, see `oriso-matrix-hardening-plan` memory) is intact. The actual gaps were (a) no standing supervisor assignment exists — `addSupervisor` is still a manual, per-session action (US#302, 2026-07-04: authority = agency-admin for their own agency) — and (b) the consent/veto question above was still open."},"355":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Decisions:**"},"356":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**New standing mechanism: \"Supervision (auto-assigned)\"** (full definition: `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md`). An agency-admin sets exactly one standing `Supervisor` per counsellor (a `Supervisor` may hold this for many counsellors). The moment that counsellor accepts any case, the assigned Supervisor auto-attaches read-only via the **existing** `SessionSupervisor`/`addSupervisor` primitive — no new access mechanism, just a standing default that removes the manual per-session step. **Purely additive**: the existing ad-hoc, per-session, manually-authorized add-supervisor flow (US#302) is unchanged and continues to exist alongside it. Rationale: reduce \"whose turn is it\" friction for training/coaching-style oversight, without touching the reach/authority model this ADR already bounded."},"357":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**No fallback on supervisor unavailability.** If the assigned Supervisor is on leave when a case is accepted, supervision simply lapses for that case — no auto-reassignment. Supervision is read-only oversight, never a precondition for the counsellor to handle the case, so nothing blocks. The agency-admin can repoint the standing assignment at any time."},"358":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Reason code: `CLINICAL_OVERSIGHT`**, not `TRAINING` — the standing relationship is ongoing oversight, not a one-off training-labeled ask."},"359":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Consent/veto — resolved, and this changes the original design:** all four Supervision reasons (`PEER_SUPPORT`, `CLINICAL_OVERSIGHT`, `SAFEGUARDING_U25`, `TRAINING`) move off the earlier binary \"consent required y/n\" split (which had only the two clinical reasons gated) onto the **same default-on, client-facing opt-out** already decided for Case Handover (`ORISO-UserService/CONTEXT.md`, \"Client opt-out mechanics\" — in-chat system-message switch, default ON, effective from the moment of switching, reversible). No Supervision reason keeps an upfront blocking consent gate under this model. This directly supersedes the \"disclose-vs-conceal is a deferred toggle\" framing in the original ADR-008 body — disclosure is no longer a passive toggle only, it is paired with an active client opt-out."},"360":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Storage (resolved 2026-07-13, implementation):** the opt-out is a nullable `is_supervision_opted_out` bit on the `session` table (entity `Session.supervisionOptedOut`, default false), added by Liquibase changeset `0066` following the idempotent `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` pattern of `0056`. Session-scoped and queryable — chosen over packing it into `session_supervisor.notes` (that column is per-supervisor, the opt-out is per-client-session) and over a separate table (unnecessary for a single boolean). Deploy caveat: clusters that force `SPRING_LIQUIBASE_ENABLED=false` (the dev cluster configmap) need the column applied manually, same as the case-handover `0057` tables."},"361":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Implementation — decision 4 (opt-out), shipped on branch `feat/supervision-consent-opt-out`, TDD:** the per-reason PENDING consent park in `SessionSupervisorFacade.addSupervisor` is deleted — every reason provisions the ADR-008 side room + client-room observation immediately. New `setSupervisionOptedOut(sessionId, optedOut)` facade method + client-guarded `POST /users/sessions/{id}/supervision/opt-out` endpoint: opting out deactivates active supervisors and kicks them from both rooms; opting back in only clears the block (no auto-reactivation — explicit re-add required). The dead consent endpoints (`.../consent`, `.../pending-consent`) + their `SecurityConfig` matchers were removed."},"362":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Implementation — decisions 1–3 (standing auto-assignment), same branch, TDD:** new `Consultant.assignedSupervisorId` (Liquibase `0067`, idempotent, no FK — a deleted supervisor degrades to a no-op attach rather than blocking the delete); kept distinct from `is_supervisor`, which remains the \"may BE a supervisor\" capability gate. `SessionSupervisorFacade.attachStandingSupervisorIfAssigned(sessionId, consultant)` attaches as `CLINICAL_OVERSIGHT` and is **best-effort by contract — it never throws**: the accept path (`AssignEnquiryFacade.assignEnquiry`) rolls the whole assignment back on any exception, so a supervision problem must degrade to \"this case is unsupervised\", never to \"the counsellor cannot accept the case\". Hooked into `assignRegisteredEnquiry` after the case is committed — **registered/Matrix only**, since Live Chat (`assignAnonymousEnquiry`) is out of supervision scope per ADR-002 and has no room to observe. The agency admin sets it via `UpdateAdminConsultantDTO.assignedSupervisorId` (validated: target must exist, be `isSupervisor`, and not be self; empty string clears)."},"363":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Not yet done (follow-ups):** the FE opt-out toggle UI; the Admin-board column UI (backend + DTO are ready); auto-attach on **re-assignment** (`AssignSessionFacade.assignSession`) and on Case-Handover takeover — currently only enquiry-accept auto-attaches, so a case that changes hands does not pick up the new counsellor's standing supervisor (open question, may be intended); the reasons endpoint still exposes the now-informational `clientConsentRequired` per reason (left intact to avoid an uncoordinated FE contract change)."},"364":{"id":"/decisions/adr-008-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-008","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-008#addendum-2026-07-13-grill-with-docs-standing-auto-assignment--unified-opt-out-consent","content":"**Still open:** cross-agency/cross-Träger scope; audit/retention sufficiency (both carried over, unchanged by this addendum)."},"365":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"page","content":"ADR-009: Global Topic/Category ownership and AI-assisted translation infrastructure","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009"},"366":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-01 (grill-with-docs session). Design decided now (\"set the points\"); implementation deliberately deferred, see Rollout below. · Datum: 2026-07-01"},"367":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"Context"},"368":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"Decision"},"369":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"370":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"371":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Rollout (deferred — do only after mid-July mandatory work)"},"372":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-01 (grill-with-docs session). Design decided now (\"set the points\"); implementation deliberately deferred, see Rollout below."},"373":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-01"},"374":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + AI (backend/frontend)"},"375":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009","content":"**Related:** `ADR-001` (Topic/Modality/Agency orthogonal axes), `ADR-003` (Department = Agency × Topic, legal-text ownership), `ADR-006` (`conversation_type` fixed enum — explicitly NOT reopened by this decision), `CONTEXT-topics-categories-departments.md`"},"376":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"Topic/Category CRUD already exists (`ORISO-ConsultingTypeService` `TopicEntity`/`TopicGroupEntity`, `ORISO-Admin` `pages/Topics`), but:"},"377":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"It is gated to `UserRole.TenantAdmin` and its `tenant_id` column, even though Topics are conceptually **global** (one unique subject, not partitioned per tenant) — the per-agency variation is the **legal text** (Department, ADR-003), not the Topic identity. This mismatch created the false impression that \"each Träger has its own topics.\""},"378":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"Translation of Topic names only happens via hand-written SQL migrations (`0011_add_english_topic_names`, `JSON_SET`/`JSON_EXTRACT` on the existing `name` JSON column) — there is no admin-facing translation UI or completeness check."},"379":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"Topic/Category icons are hardcoded frontend assets with inconsistent shape treatment (some round, some square) — no upload mechanism."},"380":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"`ADR-006`'s `conversation_type` has four fixed, structurally distinct values (Agency Counselling / Live Chat / Internal Group Chat / Self-Help Group) with no admin-editable display label or translation."},"381":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"Existing infrastructure this decision deliberately reuses rather than replacing:"},"382":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"`ORISO-Admin`'s `pages/GlobalSettings` (tabs: Login, SMTP) already stores platform-wide, non-tenant-scoped settings, including a secret credential (`globalSmtpPassword` via `FormInputPasswordField`, `useSettingsAdminMutation`)."},"383":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"`TECHNICAL_TENANT_ID = 0L` is already an established cross-service convention (AgencyService, TenantService) for \"this row is platform-level, not tenant-owned.\""},"384":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#context","content":"`TopicGroupEntity.topicEntities` is already `@ManyToMany` — a Topic can already sit in several Categories at once."},"385":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**Ownership:** Platform-Admin becomes the **exclusive** administrator of the global Topic/Category catalog (create/edit/delete Topic and Category, icon assignment, translations). Tenant-/Agency-Admins keep Department-level linking (which agency offers which topic) and author their own legal texts (DPP/Impressum, ADR-003), but no longer edit Topic/Category identity directly."},"386":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**Icon:** Topic/Category gains an admin-uploadable icon, replacing today's hardcoded, shape-inconsistent frontend assets."},"387":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**Translation-completeness validation:** the admin form warns when a configured language is missing a translation for a translatable field, instead of silently shipping a blank/fallback value."},"388":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**AI-assisted translation infrastructure:** a Platform-Admin-configurable **OpenRouter API key**, added as a new tab on the existing `GlobalSettings` page (same secret-field pattern as SMTP), used to machine-translate admin-authored text as a \"demo-quality\" starting draft — not a replacement for human review. Optionally, and only if low-effort, a translatable field/feature may carry a short fixed context string alongside the translation call (e.g. \"this is a Case Handover system notice — keep it short, plain language, no jargon\")."},"389":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**Applied to `ConversationType` labels too:** the same translation-completeness + AI-assist infrastructure covers the four fixed `ADR-006` modality display labels. The four modality **values** and their distinct code paths are unchanged — only their user-facing name per language becomes admin-editable through this infrastructure. `ADR-006` is not reopened."},"390":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#decision","content":"**Sequencing:** this ADR sets the schema/ownership direction now so the upcoming `ADR-003` Department migration (`UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)` + dedupe + Impressum column, decided the same session) doesn't need a second pass on `topic`/`agency_topic` later. Actual implementation of items 1–5 is explicitly **deferred as follow-on work after the mid-July mandatory AVV/Legal deliverables** — it is not part of that deadline."},"391":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#consequences","content":"**Positive:** one reusable translation-assist mechanism serves multiple features (Topic/Category names, ConversationType labels, and future candidates like Case Handover system-message copy) instead of a bespoke solution per feature; Platform-Admin gets clear, sole ownership of the shared taxonomy, removing the \"each tenant has its own topics\" confusion; reuses the proven `GlobalSettings` pattern instead of building a new settings surface."},"392":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** introduces an external dependency (OpenRouter) and a stored API key as a new platform-level credential to manage/rotate; AI-assisted translations are explicitly draft/demo quality and must be presented to admins as such, not as final copy; Tenant-Admins lose their current (narrow) ability to edit Topics directly, which is a permission narrowing to communicate before rollout."},"393":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#alternatives-considered","content":"**Keep per-tenant Topic catalogs as today:** rejected — perpetuates the \"each Träger has its own topics\" confusion and multiplies translation effort per tenant instead of once, globally."},"394":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#alternatives-considered","content":"**A dedicated professional translation-management integration instead of an LLM/OpenRouter key:** rejected for now — heavier integration than needed for a \"demo-quality\" starting draft; not precluded later, since the API-key field is provider-agnostic in shape."},"395":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#alternatives-considered","content":"**Let Platform-Admin define wholly new conversation types:** rejected for this decision — that collides with the still-undecided, much larger `ADR-001` \"toggleable modality module\" proposal and is explicitly out of scope here."},"396":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Migrate Topic/Category ownership UI from `UserRole.TenantAdmin`-gated to Platform-Admin-gated; keep Department-level (agency↔topic) linking on the Tenant/Agency side. Reuse existing Storybook list-view components rather than building new ones; add a preview popup so the admin sees what a Topic/Category will look like to end users before saving."},"397":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Add icon upload to Topic/Category."},"398":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Add a \"Translation\" tab to `GlobalSettings` (OpenRouter API key, optional per-feature context string), reusing `FormInputPasswordField` + `useSettingsAdminMutation`."},"399":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Add translation-completeness validation to Topic/Category admin forms."},"400":{"id":"/decisions/adr-009-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-009","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-009#rollout-deferred--do-only-after-mid-july-mandatory-work","content":"Introduce a minimal translated-label store for the 4 fixed `ConversationType` values (new small reference table or JSON blob — technical shape not yet decided, low-risk/reversible) and wire the same completeness check + AI-assist to it."},"401":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"page","content":"ADR-010: Platform-controlled per-Träger allowlist for the Erscheinungsbild (Appearance/Theme) section","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010"},"402":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010","content":"Status: Proposed — 2026-07-06 (this session); pending Frank's confirmation of the data model, then implementation. · Datum: 2026-07-06"},"403":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"Context"},"404":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"Decision (proposed)"},"405":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"406":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"407":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"Testing (what this needs)"},"408":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-010#open-pending-frank","content":"Open (pending Frank)"},"409":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010","content":"**Status:** Proposed — 2026-07-06 (this session); pending Frank's confirmation of the data model, then implementation."},"410":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-06"},"411":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"412":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010","content":"**Related:** THB theme-builder work (PRs #123/#124/#125 closed, #153 phone-preview merged 06-17, #126 THB-06 merged 07-02); `ProtectedPageLayoutWrapper.tsx` / `settingsTabs.ts` visibility gating; ORISO-Admin `GlobalSettings` (SuperAdmin-only page, login + smtp tabs); TenantService `TenantAdminControlsService` (platform-global controls singleton); memory `oriso-design-rule-disable-not-hide` (this ADR is a **deliberate, scoped exception** — see Decision §3)."},"413":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"The \"Erscheinungsbild\" (Appearance/Theme) section was reported lost after the React 19 / antd 5 modernization. Verification (2026-07-06) showed it is **not lost**: the THB theme builder (`src/pages/Tenants/Edit/ThemeSettings` → `components/Tenants/GeneralSettings` → `ThemeBuilder`, with the phone preview `iphone-14-pro.png` + `MiniChatPreview`) is intact on `dev`, byte-identical across the modernization. It is a **subsection inside the tenant edit view**, gated by role + multitenancy mode via `shouldShowThemeSettings` (`ProtectedPageLayoutWrapper.tsx:82`, `App.tsx:77`, `settingsTabs.ts:63`)."},"414":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"Two facts drive this ADR:"},"415":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"**There is already an `appearance` permission toggle** — `settings.tenantAdminControls.allowedPermissionToggles.appearance` — read in `GeneralSettings/index.tsx` (`appearanceEditable`), but it only makes the ThemeBuilder **read-only**, and it is **platform-global, not per-tenant**: `TenantAdminControlsService` loads a **single row** (`findTopByOrderByIdAsc`) and enriches *every* tenant's settings payload with the *same* controls object (comments state \"platform-global admin controls\"). So today it is all-tenants-or-none, and only read-only."},"416":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"**The requirement is per-Träger.** A platform admin (SuperAdmin) must decide, via a **multi-select of Träger**, which tenants may edit the Erscheinungsbild. Allowed → section visible and editable. Not allowed → the Erscheinungsbild subsection is **completely hidden** for that Träger."},"417":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#context","content":"SuperAdmin identity: `useUserRoles.hook.ts:39` — `AgencyAdmin && TenantAdmin && tenantId === 0`."},"418":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"**Introduce a platform-global allowlist of Träger IDs — `appearanceAllowedTenantIds: number[]` — inside the existing `tenant_admin_controls` JSON blob.** No schema migration: `controls` is `LONGTEXT` JSON, so the field is additive. This is the single authoritative source, edited only by SuperAdmin."},"419":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"**Compute the per-tenant boolean server-side.** When TenantService enriches a specific tenant's settings (`enrichSettingsWithTenantAdminControls`), set `allowedPermissionToggles.appearance = appearanceAllowedTenantIds.contains(tenantId)` for the tenant being served. This **reuses the existing boolean the frontend already reads**, and keeps the raw allowlist server-side (a tenant-admin's client only learns its own allowed/not, never the full list)."},"420":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"**Frontend: hide, do not read-only.** Change the Erscheinungsbild subsection from `readOnly` to **completely hidden** when `appearance !== true` and the user is not SuperAdmin — hide the subsection card *and* the tab/nav entry. This is a **deliberate exception** to the panel-wide \"disable, don't hide\" rule (`oriso-design-rule-disable-not-hide`): the rule governs settings a role is entitled to see but not change; here appearance editing is a **platform-granted capability** a non-allowlisted Träger has no entitlement to and should not be aware of."},"421":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"**New SuperAdmin-only multi-select** in `GlobalSettings` as a new tab (`/admin/global-settings/appearance`), listing all Träger (`searchTenantData`, label `name` / value `id`), reusing `SelectFormField` `isMulti`. Selection = `appearanceAllowedTenantIds`, saved via the existing controls update endpoint (same path as global SMTP settings). Visible/editable only for SuperAdmin."},"422":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#decision-proposed","content":"**SuperAdmin always sees and edits appearance** (bypass the allowlist), so the platform can configure any Träger's theme."},"423":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#considered-options","content":"**Per-tenant boolean column on each tenant (extend `tenant_admin_controls` with a `tenant_id`, or a new per-tenant flag).** Rejected: requires a schema migration + Liquibase changeset + per-tenant writes, for no gain over an additive JSON array."},"424":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#considered-options","content":"**Keep the single global `appearance` boolean.** Rejected: cannot express \"these Träger yes, those no.\""},"425":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#considered-options","content":"**Read-only instead of hidden.** Rejected by product: completely hide for non-allowlisted Träger."},"426":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#considered-options","content":"**Ship the full allowlist to every tenant client and filter in the browser.** Rejected: needlessly exposes the platform's full Träger allowlist to every tenant-admin; compute the per-tenant boolean on the server instead (§2)."},"427":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#consequences","content":"**Positive:** small, mostly-additive change — no DB migration (JSON field), reuses the existing global-controls service/endpoint and the existing `appearance` boolean the FE already consumes; the FE change is essentially `readOnly → hidden` plus one new SuperAdmin page; the section \"returns\" for allowlisted Träger. &#x2A;*Negative / cost:** the meaning of the existing global `appearance` boolean changes from \"global on/off\" to \"computed per served tenant from the allowlist\" — any current consumer expecting the global semantics must be checked; SuperAdmin must curate the list; a tenant newly removed from the list loses the section on next load."},"428":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"**Unit (ORISO-Admin, vitest):**"},"429":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"A pure gating helper `isAppearanceEditingAllowed({ appearanceToggle, isSuperAdmin })` (or equivalent): allowed boolean true → true; false/undefined → false; SuperAdmin → true regardless."},"430":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"Visibility: given `appearance !== true` and non-SuperAdmin, the Erscheinungsbild subsection **and** its tab/nav entry are **not rendered** (assert absence in the DOM, not merely a `readOnly` prop)."},"431":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"The SuperAdmin multi-select page renders only for SuperAdmin; a non-SuperAdmin never reaches it."},"432":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"**Unit / slice (ORISO-TenantService):**"},"433":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"`TenantAdminControlsService` round-trips `appearanceAllowedTenantIds` through the JSON `controls` (serialize/deserialize; default empty list; backward-compatible with existing rows that lack the field)."},"434":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"Enrichment computes `allowedPermissionToggles.appearance = allowlist.contains(servedTenantId)` — true for a listed tenant, false for an unlisted one; the raw list is not exposed in the enriched per-tenant payload."},"435":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"**Integration / E2E (Admin gate, Playwright/Cypress):**"},"436":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"SuperAdmin: open Global Settings → Appearance tab → multi-select lists Träger → enable a Träger → save → that Träger's admin sees and can edit the Erscheinungsbild section; disable → the section disappears for that Träger."},"437":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#testing-what-this-needs","content":"Non-SuperAdmin tenant-admin: never sees the multi-select; sees the section iff their tenant is allowlisted."},"438":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#open-pending-frank","content":"Confirm the data model (platform-global allowlist array vs. a real per-tenant flag). Recommendation: the array in the existing controls JSON (§1)."},"439":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#open-pending-frank","content":"Any existing consumer of the global `appearance` boolean that relies on global semantics (to be grepped before flipping to computed-per-tenant)."},"440":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#open-pending-frank","content":"i18n keys + exact German labels for the new tab (\"Erscheinungsbild\") and the multi-select (\"Welche Träger dürfen das Erscheinungsbild ändern?\")."},"441":{"id":"/decisions/adr-010-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-010","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-010#open-pending-frank","content":"Whether SingleTenantAdmin (single-domain mode) is ever a platform-level curator, or strictly SuperAdmin."},"442":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"page","content":"ADR-011: Helm-only deployment; single-domain path-based routing supersedes per-service subdomains","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011"},"443":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011","content":"Status: Accepted — already implemented and live on Pre-Dev. · Datum: 2026-07-07"},"444":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#context","content":"Context"},"445":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision","content":"Decision"},"446":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision-drivers","content":"Decision drivers"},"447":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"448":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"449":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-011#status--progress-2026-07-07","content":"Status & progress (2026-07-07)"},"450":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011","content":"**Status:** Accepted — already implemented and live on Pre-Dev."},"451":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-07"},"452":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011","content":"**Deciders:** Jonas Rogg / ops, announced team-wide at Jour-Fix 2026-06-30"},"453":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011","content":"**Related:** ADR-005 (Matrix keeps its own subdomain — the one deliberate exception to this decision)"},"454":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#context","content":"ORISO originally deployed via **ORISO-Kubernetes**: raw `kubectl` + Helm sub-charts, with one subdomain per surface — `app.`, `admin.`, `api.`, `auth.`, `matrix.<domain>` (still documented in that repo's README \"Access URLs\" section)."},"455":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#context","content":"Since the 2026-06-30 Jour-Fix announcement, **ORISO-Helm** is the canonical repo for all deployment, Helm charts, schemas, Keycloak, Redis, and Matrix infra changes. Its current chart already implements a different shape: `main-ingress.yaml` routes everything through **one host** (`global.domainName`) with path rules — `/` → frontend, `/admin` → Admin Panel, `/service/*` → backend APIs, `/auth` → Keycloak, `/room` → Element Call. This is not a future plan; it is already live on Pre-Dev and is the target shape for the final managed cluster on Gridscale."},"456":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#context","content":"ORISO has **no live production users** — it's a pre-launch rebuild of an older web portal, and go-live means fresh user onboarding, not a migration of live traffic. So there is no cutover risk forcing this decision, but the routing shape is still hard to change once real integrations (CORS allowlists, cookie domains, embedded links, TLS certs) depend on it."},"457":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision","content":"**ORISO-Helm, not ORISO-Kubernetes, is the single canonical definition of ORISO's deployment topology.** Every environment — including the final Gridscale-managed cluster — converges on one public domain with path-based routing, replacing the one-subdomain-per-service scheme. Matrix is the sole intentional exception and keeps its own subdomain (federation/homeserver constraints, see ADR-005)."},"458":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision-drivers","content":"One TLS certificate / one cert-manager `Issuer` instead of one per subdomain."},"459":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision-drivers","content":"No cross-origin requests between app, admin, and services — the CORS and cookie/session-domain complexity a subdomain split creates simply doesn't exist."},"460":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#decision-drivers","content":"Matches how the operator (Neusta) will actually run the final cluster: one ingress, one DNS record."},"461":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#considered-options","content":"**Keep per-service subdomains** (status quo in ORISO-Kubernetes). Rejected: needs a wildcard or N certs, and cookies still end up scoped to the parent domain anyway — the isolation subdomains promise was never really realized."},"462":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#considered-options","content":"**Hybrid** (merge app+admin, leave API/auth on subdomains). Rejected: once the CORS/cookie work is done for the merge, there's no remaining benefit to keeping any legacy subdomains — it would just perpetuate ORISO-Kubernetes as a second source of truth."},"463":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#consequences","content":"ORISO-Kubernetes's README (subdomain \"Access URLs\") is now **historical, not current** — anyone landing there for routing/ingress work should be redirected to ORISO-Helm."},"464":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#consequences","content":"ORISO-Kubernetes **cannot simply be archived**: its `.github/workflows/build-and-push.yml` is still the actual CI pipeline building and pushing every service's container image to `ghcr.io`. Until that workflow moves (into ORISO-Helm or a dedicated CI location), the repo stays alive — and PRs opened against it go nowhere in practice, confirmed by Jonas Rogg in `#oriso-dev-team`, 2026-07-07 (re: PR #84), even though the repo itself isn't marked archived on GitHub."},"465":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#consequences","content":"A pointer to this ADR was added to the top of `ORISO-Kubernetes/README.md` so the next person who lands there (as PR #84's author did) sees the redirect and the CI caveat immediately, instead of the question recurring in Slack."},"466":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#status--progress-2026-07-07","content":"Routing shape already implemented and live on Pre-Dev via `ORISO-Helm/templates/nginx/main-ingress.yaml`."},"467":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#status--progress-2026-07-07","content":"No live-migration cutover exists or is planned — the final target is simply a fresh launch on the Gridscale-managed cluster on this same scheme."},"468":{"id":"/decisions/adr-011-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-011","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-011#status--progress-2026-07-07","content":"Open blocker to archiving ORISO-Kubernetes: move `build-and-push.yml` off that repo."},"469":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"page","content":"ADR-012: Self-Help Group Chat — extend the existing Group Chat (don't rebuild), Megolm-first, future-timeline instead of a Lobby","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012"},"470":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-07-09; reconciled with live GitHub/code 2026-07-10 · Datum: 2026-07-09"},"471":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"Implementation status — 2026-07-11"},"472":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"Current verified boundary (2026-07-10)"},"473":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"Context"},"474":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"Decision"},"475":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Considered options (rejected)"},"476":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"477":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Required sequencing"},"478":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-07-09; reconciled with live GitHub/code 2026-07-10"},"479":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-09"},"480":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product + frontend) + AI (backend/architecture)"},"481":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Related:** `ADR-004-chat-keep-custom-ui-adopt-matrix-sdk-megolm.md` (hard prerequisite — real Megolm), `ADR-005-matrix-federation-off-dns-server-name.md` (clean homeserver rebuild before Megolm), WP-06 Activity Timeline (ADR-AT-01/02/03), `ORISO-Frontend/CONTEXT.md` (`Self-Help Group Chat & Lobby` glossary)"},"482":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Reference material:** `/Volumes/Netzwerkordner/001 - Archive/Step 1.png`, `Step 2.png`, `Step 4.png`, `Step 5.png`, `Step 6.png`, and `Step 7Main problem -_ repeated chats must be deleted manually.png`"},"483":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012","content":"**Implementation tracker:** `OpenResilienceInitiative/ORISO-Frontend#396`"},"484":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"Core implementation is merged into `pre-dev`: Frontend #402/#407, UserService #376/#381, and TenantService #72."},"485":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"Real-browser PreDev PASS covers Megolm text/reload, a finite weekly rollover, planned close, numeric invite/registration/assignment/join, encrypted asker messaging, dedicated two-party audio, and two-party video."},"486":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"`dev` promotion remains under human review in Frontend #406 and UserService #380."},"487":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"Additional intervals, exception edits, complex role transitions, Future Timeline variants, and the complete notification/translation matrix have unit/contract coverage but are not all independently certified by the focused E2E run. Do not collapse implemented, unit-tested, and real-browser-proven into one status."},"488":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"Reachable Email remains deliberately separate and is not implemented by this lane."},"489":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#implementation-status--2026-07-11","content":"ADR-006 #410 now owns the cross-modality persistence and regression gate before promotion."},"490":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend PR #359 and UserService PR #281 are merged: runtime chat transport is Matrix-only."},"491":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"SDK Megolm is not active. Frontend issues #332 and #346 remain open, and current `origin/dev` / `origin/pre-dev` contain no `initRustCrypto` call."},"492":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"ADR-005 remains incomplete: federation hardening was partially hot-applied on Pre-Dev, but the homeserver still uses the bare-IP `server_name`; the clean rebuild remains an ops-owned blocker."},"493":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"Matrix identity is environment-specific: Pre-Dev, the source of truth for this initiative, must use `matrix.oriso-dev.site`; Dev may use `matrix.oriso.org`. ORISO-Helm PR #32 and UserService PR #370 already provide green configurable-name/MXID regression guards; do not duplicate them. The Pre-Dev value/overlay, DNS/TLS, clean install, and runtime verification remain open."},"494":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"Frontend PR #389 was closed without merge and intentionally removed the encryption boundary; it is not a basis for this feature. Frontend PR #397 has a small Matrix-client-construction overlap for SDK logging which must be preserved when crypto initialization is added."},"495":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"All work is restricted to `pre-dev` and `dev`; repositories without either eligible branch remain untouched. No work targets `main`."},"496":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#current-verified-boundary-2026-07-10","content":"The workspace has no root `Makefile`. The design-session phrase `make verify` is intent for a real integration gate, not a currently executable command."},"497":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"The Self-Help Group Chat is not greenfield. It extends the existing Caritas Group Chat feature:"},"498":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"**UserService:** `Chat` with topic, dates, duration, recurrence, participant limit, owner, tenant-scoping agencies, `hintMessage`, and Matrix room ID; `GroupChatParticipant`; `ChatReCreator`; `DeactivateGroupChatService`."},"499":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"**Frontend:** `components/groupChat/`, `useJoinGroupChat`, the `?gcid=` login/deep-link path, `WaitingRoom`, `SessionToolbarChipFilter`, and the ElementCall group-call path."},"500":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"**Tenant/Admin:** `featureGroupChatV2Enabled` and TenantService `TranslationFacade` already exist."},"501":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"**Appointments:** UserService already integrates an external AppointmentService and stores/query-projects future appointments; the Future Timeline should use that boundary instead of inventing another local service."},"502":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#context","content":"The code still has important legacy model debt. `Chat.ChatInterval` is `WEEKLY` only; `GroupChatParticipant.chat_id` currently stores a **Session ID**, not `Chat.id`, and has no DB foreign key or role; stale-chat close uses `updateDate` plus duration/deactivation period rather than the planned `startDate + duration`; legacy `rc*` names remain in wire/database contracts even though the runtime path is Matrix-only."},"503":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Extend the existing Group Chat feature and refactor only the touched radius.** Do not rebuild it. Remove or rename remaining Rocket.Chat-era code/contracts only where a coordinated slice owns both ends."},"504":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Megolm-first.** Do not build group E2EE on the removed legacy `crypto-js` mechanism or on the inert `useE2EE` compatibility hook. Complete ADR-005, then initialize SDK/Rust crypto, then build group-chat E2EE."},"505":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Participant identity uses real Matrix accounts.** Default is the existing disposable `anon_` account; an optional persistent pseudonym supports returning participants. There is no credential-less session."},"506":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Recurrence uses a Series rule with virtual Occurrences and finite `repeatCount`.** Intervals are `DAILY`, `WEEKLY`, `BIWEEKLY`, `MONTHLY`, `QUARTERLY`, and `YEARLY`. A Matrix room is materialized only for the imminent/active occurrence. Single-date changes use an EXDATE-style skip plus a standalone one-off Series; no “this and following” split."},"507":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**The first implementation slice is an explicit Series with `repeatCount=1`.** It is finite, text-only, and non-recurring from the user's perspective: create → list → pseudonymous deep-link join → E2EE text → planned-end close."},"508":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**No separate Lobby list.** Group chats stay in Gespräche/Chats. A future extension of the same list shows upcoming group occurrences and appointments, with a draggable “now” divider plus a keyboard/toggle equivalent, bounded pagination, and existing chip filters."},"509":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Modality is a Series property:** `TEXT`, `AUDIO`, or `VIDEO`. A Matrix text room always exists; audio/video additionally use ElementCall and are opened by a counsellor."},"510":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Membership is explicit.** Roles are Owner, Co-Moderator, and Participant. The data model must define add/remove/transfer semantics before implementation; “multiple owners” and “transfer ownership” must not remain ambiguous."},"511":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Outbound communication is confidentiality-neutral.** Calendar and teaser email content carries no topic, no provider branding, and no sensitive category. Translation is limited to author-written configuration text, never chat content or PII."},"512":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#decision","content":"**Reachable email is a separate identity-layer work package.** It is global and cross-feature, not a small Group Chat UI subtask; it may be linked from the epic but should have its own owner and acceptance boundary."},"513":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Rebuild the Group Chat from scratch."},"514":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Ship group E2EE on a custom crypto layer and migrate later."},"515":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Put a Lobby into the enquiry/request flow."},"516":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Materialize an unbounded row per future occurrence."},"517":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#considered-options-rejected","content":"Support “this and following” recurrence splitting in the first release."},"518":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#consequences","content":"**Positive:** Reuses working chat, join, call, tenant, translation, and appointment paths; fixes infinite recurrence structurally; keeps the custom accessible UI; makes real Matrix E2EE a prerequisite instead of future debt."},"519":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#consequences","content":"**Cost / risk:** The feature is blocked on ops and crypto work; the existing Series/Session/participant schema needs an explicit migration contract; the future list combines two sources; role transitions and key rotation interact; current integration-test wording references a nonexistent command and must be replaced by a real harness."},"520":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-50","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"ADR-005 clean homeserver rebuild with stable DNS `server_name`."},"521":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-51","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"SDK/Rust Megolm initialization, encrypted-room creation, key backup/recovery, and multi-device verification."},"522":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-52","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Contract/model slice: Series/Occurrence/Exception schema, role semantics, planned-end close, and an executable integration gate."},"523":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-53","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"First vertical slice (`repeatCount=1`, text only)."},"524":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-54","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Recurrence and occurrence edits."},"525":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-55","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Explicit roles/invites and modality."},"526":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-56","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Future Timeline and Activity Timeline integration."},"527":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-57","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Waiting Area, multilingual author config, calendar, and notification polish."},"528":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-58","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Separate reachable-email work package."},"529":{"id":"/decisions/adr-012-59","page_id":"/decisions/adr-012","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-012#required-sequencing","content":"Each slice follows red-green TDD, relevant repository integration tests, the frontend unit/lint/build hard gate, Playwright/real-browser verification, mobile and desktop checks, fresh-user proof, and Pre-Dev validation when deployment is in scope."},"530":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","type":"page","content":"ADR-013 — 2FA via vendored otp-config SPI (not stock-Keycloak AIA)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-013"},"531":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013","content":"Status: Accepted · Date: 2026-07-11 · Datum: 2026-07-11"},"532":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-013#context","content":"Context"},"533":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-013#options","content":"Options"},"534":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-013#decision","content":"Decision"},"535":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-013#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"536":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013","content":"**Status:** Accepted · &#x2A;*Date:** 2026-07-11\n&#x2A;*Context docs:** `PLAN-2fa-otp-enablement-2026-07-11.md`\n&#x2A;*PRs:** ORISO-Helm #55, ORISO-UserService #392"},"537":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#context","content":"ORISO's 2FA feature is fully built on both ends — the frontend ships a complete\nsetup wizard (QR code, TOTP app, email OTP, login OTP field) and the\nUserService exposes the four `/users/2fa` endpoints — but both are clients of\nthe onlineBeratung **otp-config Keycloak SPI**, which was never deployed: the\nplatform runs the stock `quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.3` image. The\nUserService swallows the SPI failure and reports `twoFactorAuth.isEnabled =\nfalse`, which silently hides the whole feature. Flipping the\n`identity.otp-allowed-*` flags therefore had no visible effect."},"538":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#context","content":"A constraint floated during triage was \"no custom Keycloak image/provider\".\nThat collides with a hard platform fact: **Keycloak's Admin REST API cannot\ncreate OTP credentials** (read and delete only). Any design keeping QR-code\nsetup inside the ORISO UI needs either the SPI or unsupported DB writes."},"539":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#options","content":"**A — vendor the SPI (chosen).** Port\n`Onlineberatung/onlineberatung-keycloak-otp` (AGPL, same upstream family as\nall ORISO services) to Keycloak 26.6.3 and ship it as a thin image layer.\nThe port turned out minimal: one API replacement\n(`CredentialHelper.deleteOTPCredential` → `removeStoredCredentialById`), one\ntest-scope dependency, all 53 upstream unit tests green. The SPI also ships\nthe direct-grant authenticators that return the `{otpType}` challenge JSON the\nfrontend already parses, and enables email OTP end to end (setup mail +\nlogin-time codes) — feature parity with upstream Caritas."},"540":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#options","content":"**B — stock Keycloak + Application-Initiated Action.** Admin REST for\nstatus/disable, browser redirect to `kc_action=CONFIGURE_TOTP` for setup.\nRejected because: the built wizard would be discarded for a Keycloak-themed\npage; direct-grant login means no Keycloak SSO cookie, so users would re-enter\ncredentials during setup; stock Keycloak has no email OTP; and the UserService\nOTP adapter plus the frontend panel would need rewrites. Strictly worse UX at\nhigher cost, saved only a 3-line Dockerfile."},"541":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#decision","content":"Vendor the SPI source into `ORISO-Helm/keycloak-image/otp-config-spi/`\n(provenance and local patches documented in its README), build\n`ghcr.io/openresilienceinitiative/oriso-keycloak` in CI, and bind the\n`direct-grant-2fa` flow in `realm.json` (fresh imports) plus\n`scripts/keycloak-apply-2fa-flow.sh` (existing realms). The \"no custom image\"\nwish is dropped as based on a wrong premise; the image is a 3-line layer over\nstock, rebuilt by CI like every other ORISO image."},"542":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#consequences","content":"2FA works with the designed in-app UX for app-TOTP and email OTP; per-role\nflags control exposure (Pre-Dev: consultants + tenant admins)."},"543":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#consequences","content":"We own a small vendored SPI and must re-verify it on Keycloak upgrades\n(`mvn test` in CI covers this on every touch; the port surface has been one\nmethod so far)."},"544":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#consequences","content":"Prod rollout requires Neusta coordination (they operate prod Keycloak)."},"545":{"id":"/decisions/adr-013-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-013","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-013#consequences","content":"The invite-flow two-factor gate becomes real: OTP activation flips\n`PENDING_SETUP → ACTIVE`, deletion re-opens it, and admins can waive with a\nrecorded reason (four-eyes onboarding stays possible without 2FA hardware)."},"546":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","type":"page","content":"ADR-014: Shared legal-text objects, multi-topic agencies, and topic-before-consent","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-014"},"547":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-16 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-07-16"},"548":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"Context"},"549":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"Decision"},"550":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-014#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"551":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-014#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"552":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-16 (grill-with-docs session)"},"553":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-16"},"554":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"> **Number collision resolved 2026-08-08 (ORISO-Docs#73).** A second accepted ADR also carried\n> the number 014 (media scanning via the Matrix content scanner). It was the later decision\n> (2026-07-18) and became **ADR-019**. This record keeps 014, so an unqualified \"ADR-014\" now\n> means shared legal text objects and topic-before-consent."},"555":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"> **Extended 2026-08-16 by `ADR-021`.** Nothing here is reversed. ADR-021 adds what this record\n> does not cover: the **platform level above the Träger**, a **generic version history** for legal\n> texts (today only the AVV has one), and the **consent sentence as a field of the DPP**. The\n> topic-before-consent invariant below is unchanged and is the reason Gate 2 in `ADR-022` can\n> resolve a department document at all."},"556":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"**Deciders:** Frank + AI"},"557":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014","content":"**Related:** `ADR-003` (Department = unique Agency × Topic — **partially superseded by this ADR**, see below);\n`ADR-021` (hierarchy, versioning, consent text — extends this record); `ADR-022` (consent gates);\n`ADR-009` (global Topic ownership); `CONTEXT-topics-categories-departments.md`;\n`CONTEXT-domain-caritas-diakonie-online-counselling.md` (Org → Tenancy Mapping);\nQDL epic ORISO-Frontend#181 (QR code & direct links)"},"558":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"ADR-003 correctly made the Department = unique (agency\\_id, topic\\_id) the carrier of the\nindividualised Impressum + DPP. But two of its implementation choices turned out to violate the\nresult the domain actually needs:"},"559":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"**The single-select admin topic picker** (ADR-003 decision #3, shipped as ORISO-Admin PR #244)\nforces one topic per agency. Real Beratungsstellen host several independent Fachbereiche under\none roof; modelling that as one agency per topic would multiply the same real-world entity\n(same address maintained N times) and corrupt any future resource management. The DB never\nforbade multi-topic agencies — `UNIQUE(agency_id, topic_id)` only forbids the *same* topic\ntwice. The QDL direct-link epic (#181/#184, \"restrict topic options to `agency.topicIds`\")\nalso presupposes multi-topic agencies."},"560":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"**Inline legal-text storage** (the 2026-07-07 reconcile: keep `agency_topic.content_dpp` /\n`content_imprint` inline, drop the `dpp_id`/`imprint_id` references) makes sharing impossible:\none DPP that legally covers four Fachbereiche must be pasted and maintained four times — the\nsame duplication disease at the text level."},"561":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"Additionally, the QDL direct-link flow (QDL-02, #183) planned the topic pop-up *after* account\ncreation — but privacy consent happens *during* account creation, and the department-specific\nDPP/Impressum can only be resolved once (agencyId, topicId) are known. Choosing the topic after\nconsent means the client consented to the wrong (tenant-fallback) document."},"562":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"Three invariants drive this decision (Frank, 2026-07-16):"},"563":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"**No duplicated real-world entities.** One Beratungsstelle = one agency row, however many\ntopics it serves."},"564":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"**Flexible legal-text assignment.** One text may cover many Fachbereiche, or each may have its\nown — an authoring decision, not a schema constraint; never maintained in N copies."},"565":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#context","content":"**Unambiguous consent.** It must always be clear which counselling body a consultant belongs to\nand exactly which legal texts the help-seeker consents to."},"566":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"**Agencies are multi-topic again.** The admin topic picker returns to **multi-select**\n(reverses ADR-003 decision #3 / ORISO-Admin PR #244). Existing multi-topic agencies are\n**valid data**, not dirt to clean up. Department = unique (agency × topic), the `UNIQUE`\nconstraint, and the draft|published lifecycle from ADR-003 all stand unchanged."},"567":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"**Legal texts become first-class shared objects.** New `legal_text` entity\n(id, tenant\\_id, kind = DPP | IMPRINT, label, multilingual content, publication\\_status).\n`agency_topic` references them via &#x2A;*nullable `dpp_id` / `imprint_id`** (reverses the\n2026-07-07 \"keep inline, drop references\" reconcile). Several departments may point at the\nsame text; editing a shared text warns \"used by N departments\" and offers fork-as-copy."},"568":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"**Migration is additive:** lift existing inline `content_dpp`/`content_imprint` into\n`legal_text` rows, merge byte-identical texts into one shared row, set the references; keep\nthe inline columns as read-fallback for one release, then drop them."},"569":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"**Unassigned = tenant fallback.** A department without an assigned text falls back to the\ntenant-level document (today's behaviour). No auto-created empty drafts."},"570":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#decision","content":"**Topic-before-consent invariant:** in every registration path — normal flow and all QDL\ndirect links (`cid`/`aid`/`tid`) — **agency + topic (= the department) must be determined\nbefore the consent step**, so the consent screen always shows the correct department\nDPP/Impressum. Concretely: a counsellor link without `tid` shows the topic pop-up as the\n*first* screen after opening the link (QDL-02 order corrected); per-topic links/QR codes\n(`aid`+`tid`, `cid`+`tid`) are the department-level variant and skip the pop-up."},"571":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#consequences","content":"**Positive:** no phantom duplicate agencies (addresses maintained once; resource management stays\naccurate); \"one text for four Fachbereiche\" is a pointer, not four copies; consent is always\nagainst the resolvable department document; the QDL epic's center QR (`aid`) and department QR\n(`aid`+`tid`) map 1:1 onto the model; the client-side `DepartmentLegalSection` keeps working\nunchanged (only the backend resolution source changes)."},"572":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** reverses two already-merged pieces of work (Admin #244 single-select; the\ninline-text reconcile in AgencyService `0021`/`0023`); a new entity + admin surface\n(legal-text library, per-department assignment) must be built; a backfill/dedup migration is\nrequired; QDL-02 (#183) must reorder its pop-up."},"573":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#alternatives-considered","content":"**One agency per topic (\"Design B\"):** rejected — duplicates the same physical Beratungsstelle\nper topic, multiplies address maintenance, and fabricates entities that do not exist in the\nreal world, corrupting resource management."},"574":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#alternatives-considered","content":"**Keep inline per-department texts:** rejected — sharing one legally identical text across\ndepartments degenerates into N maintained copies; exactly the duplication the domain forbids."},"575":{"id":"/decisions/adr-014-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-014","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-014#alternatives-considered","content":"**Topic selection after consent (QDL-02 as originally specced):** rejected — the client would\nconsent before the applicable department document is knowable."},"576":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","type":"page","content":"ADR-015 — Per-chat-type media flag families replace `featureAttachmentUploadDisabled`","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-015"},"577":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015","content":"Status: Accepted · Date: 2026-07-18 · Datum: 2026-07-18"},"578":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-015#context","content":"Context"},"579":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-015#options","content":"Options"},"580":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-015#decision","content":"Decision"},"581":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-015#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"582":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015","content":"**Status:** Accepted · &#x2A;*Date:** 2026-07-18\n&#x2A;*Context docs:** `PLAN-media-upload-security-2026-07-18.md`"},"583":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#context","content":"Media handling needs three orthogonal switches (upload allowed; inline display\nvs file-only download with virus scan attached; AI scan on/off), each\nconfigurable **per chat type** (1:1 / group / anonymous live chat / supervision)\nand on **every level** of the settings cascade (platform governance → tenant →\nagency), like every other ORISO base capability."},"584":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#context","content":"Today there is exactly one related switch: `featureAttachmentUploadDisabled` —\nan **inverted** flag, tenant/agency level only, **no chat-type granularity**,\nedited under Communication Settings, read by the Frontend to hide the upload\nbutton. It directly overlaps the new upload switch."},"585":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#context","content":"The existing pattern for per-chat-type capabilities is the\n`featureVideoCalls*` family: a master flag plus four chat-type-suffixed\nvariants, present in `TenantSettings` and the agency `settings` JSON with\nidentical vocabulary, capped platform-side via `allowedPermissionToggles`\n(`tenant_admin_controls` / `agency_admin_control`), rendered as chat-type cards\nin the Admin."},"586":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#options","content":"**A — replace (chosen).** New `featureMediaUpload*` family supersedes the old\nflag entirely: one-time translation of stored tenant/agency settings (old\n\"disabled\" → new family off everywhere), old switch removed from Admin UI and\nFrontend. One source of truth; the new family's master flag *is* the kill\nswitch. No production users exist, so migration risk is minimal."},"587":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#options","content":"**B — keep both.** Old flag stays as a global kill switch next to the granular\nfamily. Two overlapping switches whose interaction nobody can explain later;\npermanent confusion in the Admin."},"588":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#decision","content":"Introduce three flag families following the `featureVideoCalls*` pattern\nverbatim — `featureMediaUpload…`, `featureMediaInlineDisplay…`,\n`featureMediaAiScan…` (master + four chat-type variants each) — on tenant *and*\nagency level, with new platform `allowedPermissionToggles` keys, and &#x2A;*remove\n`featureAttachmentUploadDisabled`** via a one-time, TDD-covered settings\ntranslation. Chat type is the only dimension; there is no separate\nlogged-in/anonymous axis (anonymous users exist only in the anonymous live chat\ntype)."},"589":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#decision","content":"The migration is written test-first and must prove: existing stored settings\ntranslate correctly, Frontend behaviour is identical pre/post for every\ncombination, and no tenant loses its current upload posture."},"590":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#consequences","content":"Admins configure media behaviour per chat type like video calls — familiar UI,\nno new concepts."},"591":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#consequences","content":"Every consumer of `featureAttachmentUploadDisabled` (Admin Communication\nSettings, Frontend message submit interface, generated API types) must be\nmigrated in the same change set; the flag disappears from the API surface."},"592":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#consequences","content":"3 families × 5 flags × 2 levels + governance keys is a wide but shallow\nsurface — the cost of \"configurable down to the smallest unit\", accepted\ndeliberately."},"593":{"id":"/decisions/adr-015-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-015","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-015#consequences","content":"Requires the agency-level settings UI (WP-0) so the agency dimension is\nactually operable, not just stored."},"594":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","type":"page","content":"ADR-016: Team-Besprechung — separate side room per open enquiry, hard close at acceptance","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-016"},"595":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-18 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-07-18"},"596":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-016#context","content":"Context"},"597":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"Decision"},"598":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-016#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"599":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-016#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"600":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-18 (grill-with-docs session)"},"601":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-18"},"602":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"603":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016","content":"**Related:** ADR-002 (silent membership / access curtain), ADR-008 (supervision side-channel = separate room), `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md` (Team-Besprechung overlay), `ORISO-Frontend/CONTEXT.md` (full glossary entry), memory `oriso-team-besprechung-design`"},"604":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#context","content":"Counsellor teams want to coordinate on an incoming enquiry (\"who takes this, what do you think?\") before anyone accepts it — invisible to the advice seeker — and then continue the normal 1:1. The tempting implementation is \"hidden messages / a team thread inside the client's conversation\", but Matrix delivers every event to every room member's device: in-room hiding was exactly the U25 safeguarding leak ADR-008 removed. Verified on `origin/pre-dev`: the ADR-008 side-room primitive is alive (per-session Matrix room the client is never invited to, leak-abort on the send path), but it attaches at *acceptance* and assumes an assigned consultant; the old Caritas Feedback-Chat was physically removed (changeset 0046)."},"605":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"**Team-Besprechung = a separate Matrix room attached to one open Agency-Counselling enquiry**, generalizing the ADR-008 side-room principle to the pre-assignment phase. Guardrail (hard rule): &#x2A;*team coordination never happens in the client's room — not even \"hidden\".**"},"606":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"**Hard close at acceptance.** The moment the enquiry is accepted, the Besprechung is archived — it is *not* carried into the active case. Post-acceptance coordination uses the existing mechanisms: **Supervision** (read-only accompaniment) or **Case Handover** (co-access/takeover). This keeps three cleanly separated coordination tools instead of one blurry one."},"607":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"**Archive re-access is read-only** (hard rule); access rules stay loose for now (team members may look without a co-access ceremony); retention rides the existing archive auto-deletion — no new TTL mechanism."},"608":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"**Participation right = enquiry visibility right.** Exactly the counsellors who can see (and could accept) the enquiry may discuss; no new permission layer. A tenant-level feature toggle guards the whole feature."},"609":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"**The discussion is flat** — the side room is already scoped to one enquiry, so it *is* the one \"thread on the enquiry\"; no thread machinery inside it. Scope: Agency Counselling only (Live Chat is anonymous/ephemeral and excluded per ADR-002; the other modalities have no request area)."},"610":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#decision","content":"UI: a panel/tab on the enquiry in the request area, with a post-count badge and a permanent \"team-only — invisible to the advice seeker\" marker, so a counsellor is never unsure which side they are writing on."},"611":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#considered-options","content":"**Thread in the client's room, hidden client-side.** Rejected: impossible to hide on Matrix; re-opens the ADR-008 leak class."},"612":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#considered-options","content":"**Carry the side room into the active case.** Rejected by product decision: post-accept coordination belongs to Supervision/Case Handover; a room that lives on blurs that boundary. Context continuity is served by read-only archive access instead (\"frozen, on demand\" rather than \"open forever\")."},"613":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#considered-options","content":"**Wait for Megolm per-recipient subsets (one room, cryptographic hiding).** Deferred in ADR-008 already; unrealistic before go-live 2026-10-01."},"614":{"id":"/decisions/adr-016-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-016","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-016#consequences","content":"**Positive:** reuses a shipped, leak-guarded primitive; no new permission model; clean lifecycle boundary matching the existing mechanism taxonomy. &#x2A;*Cost:** room provisioning at enquiry time (pre-assignment operator handling — today's facade assumes an assigned consultant); notification recipient fan-out must be built (current message producers hardcode user+consultant); archived-room re-access UI."},"615":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","type":"page","content":"ADR-017: Rebuild chat threads on native Matrix `m.thread` relations — hard cut, no dual-read","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-017"},"616":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-18 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-07-18"},"617":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-017#context","content":"Context"},"618":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-017#decision","content":"Decision"},"619":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-017#considered-options","content":"Considered options"},"620":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-017#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"621":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-18 (grill-with-docs session)"},"622":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-18"},"623":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"624":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017","content":"**Related:** ADR-004 (keep own UI, adopt Matrix SDK), ADR-016 (Team-Besprechung is flat — does not depend on this), memory `feedback-no-prod-users-skip-migration`, memory `oriso-team-besprechung-design`"},"625":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017#context","content":"Audit of `origin/pre-dev` (2026-07-18): the existing threads feature is **fully custom** — thread membership is carried as a plaintext token `[THREAD:<rootEventId>]` prepended to the message body (`messageConstants.ts`), parsed back out client-side per message. There is zero use of MSC3440 / matrix-js-sdk native threads, although the shipped SDK (v38) supports them completely. Consequences: no interop (other Matrix clients see the raw token), summaries/counts only over currently-loaded messages, no thread pagination, no per-thread read receipts, association breaks on root edit/redaction. Frank wants threads extended, so the base must become sound first."},"626":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017#decision","content":"Migrate the send **and** read path to native Matrix threads (`m.relates_to: { rel_type: \"m.thread\", event_id, is_falling_back: true, \"m.in_reply_to\": … }`; UI driven by `room.getThreads()` / `Thread` timelines / threaded receipts). &#x2A;*Hard cut:** the `[THREAD:]` prefix convention and its parser are deleted entirely — no dual-read compatibility path. Pre-existing prefix messages render as ordinary flat messages; a minimal render filter strips any leftover visible `[THREAD:…]` token from message bodies (cosmetic only, no thread semantics attached)."},"627":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017#considered-options","content":"**Extend the custom prefix system.** Rejected: reimplements what the SDK provides, keeps all listed defects, and adds more `[THREAD:]` legacy data the longer it lives."},"628":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017#considered-options","content":"**Dual-read transition (native first, prefix fallback).** Rejected under the house rule \"no prod users → don't carry migration burdens\": pre-dev data is disposable, and the parser is precisely the legacy we want gone. Two permanent read paths for disposable data is a bad trade."},"629":{"id":"/decisions/adr-017-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-017","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-017#consequences","content":"**Positive:** Element-grade thread capabilities (thread list, pagination, per-thread unread/receipts, cross-client interop) become available from the SDK instead of hand-built; the custom notification endpoints (`thread.reply.new` etc.) remain as an overlay and keep working. &#x2A;*Cost:** existing pre-dev thread conversations flatten (accepted — no production users); the send path (`matrixClientService.sendMessage`) and read path (prefix parsing → `event.getThread()`) are a real rebuild, not an incremental patch."},"630":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","type":"page","content":"ADR-018: Erstantwort — one persisted event rendered as a Carimat bubble sequence, configured per Träger","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-018"},"631":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-30 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-07-30"},"632":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"Context"},"633":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"Decision"},"634":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Delivery cut"},"635":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-018#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"636":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-07-30 (grill-with-docs session)"},"637":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"**Date:** 2026-07-30"},"638":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"639":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"**Related:** `CONTEXT-erstantwort-und-carimat.md` (full glossary), ADR-003 + `ADR-014-shared-legal-text-objects-multi-topic-agencies-topic-before-consent.md` (Fachbereich owns DPP/Impressum; topic before consent), ADR-004/ADR-005 (Matrix + Megolm), ADR-008 (who reads along), ADR-010 (platform-controlled per-tenant allowlist — the same shape, deferred here), `CONTEXT-conversation-types.md`, `ORISO-Frontend/CONTEXT.md` (Activity Timeline), ORISO-Frontend issue #772"},"640":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018","content":"**Trigger:** U25 supplied a first-response text that deviates drastically from the platform default — informal, gender-free, \"we counsel by MAIL and are NOT a chat service\", a peer-counselling and supervision disclosure, an explicit \"do not send us personal data\" and therefore **no** invitation to leave an e-mail address, plus emergency numbers. Björn's open questions to Janna (2026-07-24) asked whether such a message must become per-agency configurable."},"641":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"Retiring the Rocket.Chat transport (ADR-004) took the first-response posting with it, and nothing replaced it. Verified on `origin/pre-dev`: `postWelcomeMessageIfConfigured`, `postFurtherStepsIfConfigured` and `FURTHER_STEPS` have **zero occurrences** in UserService `src/main`, and `createEnquiryMessage` delegates unconditionally to `createMatrixEnquiryMessage`. What survived is the scaffolding around the removed mechanism:"},"642":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"The **configuration without its mechanism**: `welcomeMessage.sendWelcomeMessage` + `welcomeMessageText` (per-Träger free text, default off, Admin form field never built) and `sendFurtherStepsMessage` (default on) still exist and now toggle nothing."},"643":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"The **renderer without its transport**: `FurtherSteps.tsx` renders only when `alias.messageType === 'FURTHER_STEPS'`, and no Matrix code path produces an `alias` object. The frontend still targets `/service/messages/...`; UserService on `origin/pre-dev` has **no** `PATCH /messages/{id}` handler, and no `messageservice` deployment exists in the Pre-Dev manifests while `MESSAGE_SERVICE_API_URL` still points at one. Both call sites swallow their errors silently, which is why this stayed invisible."},"644":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"Measured on Pre-Dev 2026-07-30 (`api.oriso-dev.site`): `GET /service/messages/` answers **401 with a Bearer challenge**, like the routed control `/service/users/data`, while an unknown path answers 404 — so the path is *not* unrouted and *not* an SPA fallthrough, contrary to what earlier drafts of this ADR and of the linked issues claimed. Those drafts reasoned from the ORISO-Helm chart, which **Pre-Dev does not run** (`values-pre-dev.yaml` header: Pre-Dev still runs the archived ORISO-Kubernetes release, ORISO-Helm#110) — a trap worth remembering for any future infrastructure claim about Pre-Dev. Whether an *authenticated* `PATCH` reaches a handler is untested and must not be assumed either way."},"645":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"`TopicEntity.welcomeMessage` / `sendNextStepMessage` exist per Fachbereich with **no consumer anywhere**."},"646":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"Meanwhile a Carimat persona *is* shipped (robot avatar, name, subtitle line above the bubble) in the pseudonym/privacy onboarding, together with the animation primitives (`TypingReveal`, `TypewriterText`) and a multi-bubble precedent (the three breathing cards). The only surviving in-chat consent surface carries `role=\"dialog\" aria-modal=\"true\"` although it is an inline card, and it blocks the ratsuchende person's composer. Its promise (\"Erst danach dürfen unsere Berater\\_innen einen Chat mit ihnen starten\") **does hold**: the gate is active exactly while the session is `STATUS_EMPTY`/`STATUS_ENQUIRY`, so nothing has been sent and nobody has picked the case up. No server-side check of `dataPrivacyConfirmation` exists, but that is a hardening gap against a bypassed client, not a false statement."},"647":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#context","content":"Naively \"making the message editable per agency\" would therefore paste a Träger's prose over a mechanism that does not run, drop two working action buttons, drop the formal/informal axis, and turn statements the system can verify (who reads along, which modality, which deadline) into unverifiable typed claims — in the one document that is supposed to serve as the KDG §11 transparency record."},"648":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**The Erstantwort is composed from Bausteine, not authored as one text.** A fixed platform catalogue of \\~15 units, each with a trigger, a source (Plattform-Text / Träger-Text / derived), an optional action, a modality assignment, and a toggle. Rejected both extremes: a hard-coded message (would need a release per Träger) and a free rich-text field (loses the action buttons and turns verifiable facts into claims)."},"649":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Exactly one free Baustein.** A single per-Träger \"Freier Hinweis\" at a fixed position is the deliberate escape hatch — U25's peer-counselling disclosure lands there. Guardrail: &#x2A;*derived Bausteine are never editable.** What the system knows, the system renders; a typed claim can contradict the configuration, a rendered one cannot."},"650":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Delivery = one persisted `[SYSTEM_NOTIFICATION]` event with a versioned structured payload**, rendered client-side as a staged bubble sequence with typing dots. &#x2A;*Carimat is a rendering identity, not a Matrix account.** A bot account in the room would be an additional Megolm key holder in a room holding §11 KDG special-category data, and a bot has no Schweigepflicht — so either the operator gains a technical read path (and the zero-data-emission claim falls), or the bot sends plaintext into an encrypted room. Neither is acceptable. A purely client-side sequence was also rejected: it would leave **no evidence** that the person was told the deadline, the confidentiality terms, who reads along, and the emergency numbers — precisely what a supervisory authority asks about for a service with real minors."},"651":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Frozen words, live state.** The event stores the resolved wording (so what was said is provable and later configuration changes do not rewrite history); completion is read live from state that **already exists** (`displayName`, `dataPrivacyConfirmation`, `email`, 2FA) through endpoints that already work. Consequence, accepted deliberately: a Baustein whose completion is *not* already represented elsewhere does not belong in this catalogue — the Case-Handover team-access opt-out switch from `ORISO-UserService/CONTEXT.md` is therefore explicitly **out of scope** here, even though it looks like a sibling."},"652":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Ordering belongs to the platform, content to the Träger.** Each Baustein's trigger (chat entry · after the first message · after the enquiry was dispatched · after assignment) is platform-assigned, because consent must precede data transmission and no Träger may reorder that by accident."},"653":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Editorial content hangs at Träger level; resolution is a chain from day one.** `Fachbereich ?? Beratungsstelle ?? Träger ?? Plattform` is implemented immediately, but only the Träger level gets an Admin UI — the middle levels become a form later, not a migration. U25 is its own Träger, so this covers the trigger case. Each Baustein also carries a \"platform-permitted\" field pre-set to *yes*, so the two-level permission model (ADR-010's shape) is likewise a later UI. &#x2A;*Interim safety measure instead of that model:** the two safety-bearing Bausteine — \"send us no personal data\" and the emergency numbers — get **no toggle at all** for now."},"654":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**The platform's own voice is gender-neutral by reformulation**, not by notation. Rejected a Träger-selectable notation axis: the actual request is the *absence* of gendered terms, notation × 7 locales × formal/informal is a combinatorial and machine-translation dead end, and German notation has no counterpart in the six other locales. Scope now: every text where the platform speaks for itself (the person reads them consecutively from one sender — a mixed notation is a contradiction inside one conversation, not a style blemish in two documents). The remaining UI is a separate sweep. This also resolves the shipped inconsistency between `Berater*in` and `Berater_innen`."},"655":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**A Träger writes one German variant**, chosen by its existing `languageFormal`; only Plattform-Texte carry both. Translation is **optional** and machine-assisted on publish, reusing the legal-texts mechanism; a missing locale falls back to the original, with English as second choice. Rejected requiring all seven locales (nobody would ever publish) and German-only (U25's core statements — peer counselling, send no personal data, emergency numbers — would silently vanish for every non-German-speaking person on a suicide-prevention service)."},"656":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**Forward lock yes, backward lock no.** The composer stays blocked until consent is confirmed — which today is what actually guarantees the promise, since the gate is active only in the pre-assignment enquiry phase. A server-side check of `dataPrivacyConfirmation` is added on top as defence in depth, scoped to entry paths where the person did not choose the agency beforehand (in Agency Counselling consent is given at registration per ADR-014 *shared legal text objects*), together with a regression test pinning the flow invariant so a later refactor cannot remove the protection silently. No Baustein ever blocks assignment or a counsellor's reply; e-mail, 2FA and credential saving are voluntary throughout."},"657":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**The send confirmation is hollowed out**: it acknowledges dispatch and no longer names the deadline, which now has exactly one owner. It closes when the first bubble is up rather than after a fixed 10 s."},"658":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#decision","content":"**One Activity Timeline entry** for the whole Erstantwort, targeting the chat — which requires a deliberate exception to the current filter that discards system notifications. Rejected one entry per open action: a person who has just sent a first message about suicidal thoughts should not receive three to-do items."},"659":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Issue #772 is **repurposed, not closed** (it carries a stakeholder and a live conversation thread) and becomes the **first slice** under a new EPIC: the Baustein sequence with platform defaults only — gender-neutral wording, hollowed-out send confirmation, one Activity Timeline entry, action Bausteine reading existing state. **No Admin UI and no Träger texts in the first slice**, which is what makes it independent of Janna's pending answers: everything still open concerns Träger content."},"660":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Sibling issues under the EPIC:"},"661":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Admin UI + Träger texts (the per-Träger editor, reusing the legal-texts editor and its machine translation)"},"662":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Konto-vervollständigen Baustein — display name plus optional e-mail, triggered after the enquiry was dispatched"},"663":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"The chat bubble with **all** existing variants and alignments in Storybook, plus the variants designed here (`FurtherSteps`, `SystemMessage`, `ReassignMessage`, `E2EEActivatedMessage`, the Case-Handover cards and the Carimat cards have no stories today)"},"664":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"The Admin card for display-name editing and optional e-mail — as the **first** card under Einstellungen/Berechtigungen, modelled on `CaseHandoverCard`; it also has to fix the existing \"Login-Funktion\" card, whose description promises behaviour that does not exist"},"665":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Credential saving: repair the browser save prompt at registration (`name` attributes, do not cut the prompt off with the hard redirect) plus \"set your password now\" after the enquiry, verified in Safari, Firefox and Chromium"},"666":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Server-side enforcement of `dataPrivacyConfirmation` on the assign and reply paths"},"667":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#delivery-cut","content":"Reconcile `handover.mdx` with the code and with the 2026-07-06 opt-out decision"},"668":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#consequences","content":"**Positive.** The first slice ships without waiting on Janna's answers, because everything still open concerns Träger texts, which arrive in a later slice. No new key holder in any counselling room. No new state, no new table, no resurrection of MessageService — every action reuses a working routed endpoint. The catalogue makes U25's text expressible without a release, and switching off the e-mail invitation is a toggle rather than a text deletion, so the contradiction Janna objected to disappears structurally."},"669":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#consequences","content":"**Cost.** A structured payload needs versioning, or a later frontend renders old events wrongly. A foreign Matrix client sees a JSON blob instead of bubbles. Neutral reformulation is genuine copywriting, not search-and-replace, and reads flatter than the gendered original. Roughly fifteen Bausteine × several locales is real editorial surface. The Activity-Timeline filter exception and the server-side consent check are both new backend work that #772 did not previously contain."},"670":{"id":"/decisions/adr-018-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-018","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-018#consequences","content":"**Surfaced but not decided here.** The **Wiederherstellungslücke** — no e-mail means no recovery, and the generated 16-character password is never shown again — is a structural consequence of the anonymity model rather than a fault, but it is written down nowhere and has no row in `edge-cases.mdx`. Note that the reset endpoint's uninformative response is **deliberate** account-enumeration protection and must be preserved. One candidate shape for a recovery path is a recovery code at registration, following the shipped Matrix recovery-key flow; \"no recovery, credential saving is the mitigation\" is an equally legitimate outcome. Either way the decision belongs in its own record, not here. Cross-browser credential saving must be **verified** in Safari, Firefox and Chromium rather than assumed: the Credential Management API is Chromium-only, and the registration flow's `preventDefault()` + XHR + hard `window.location.href` is not a form submission that Safari or Firefox recognise. Separately, `handover.mdx` §4.7.3/§4.7.7 documents in-chat consent buttons the code does not have and predates the 2026-07-06 opt-out decision; and two accepted ADRs both carry the number **014**."},"671":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","type":"page","content":"ADR-019 — Media scanning via matrix-content-scanner, fail-closed, pluggable AI check","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-019"},"672":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019","content":"Status: Accepted · Date: 2026-07-18 · Datum: 2026-07-18"},"673":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"Context"},"674":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-019#options","content":"Options"},"675":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"Decision"},"676":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-019#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"677":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019","content":"**Status:** Accepted · &#x2A;*Date:** 2026-07-18"},"678":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019","content":"> **Renumbered 2026-08-08 from ADR-014 (ORISO-Docs#73).** Two accepted ADRs both carried\n> the number 014, so every cross-reference to \"ADR-014\" was ambiguous. The later of the two —\n> this one, accepted 2026-07-18 — took the new number; `ADR-014-shared-legal-text-objects-…`\n> (accepted 2026-07-16) keeps 014. Inbound references in `0 - Docs` were updated with it."},"679":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019","content":"**Context docs:** `PLAN-media-upload-security-2026-07-18.md`"},"680":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"ORISO adds image upload to both TipTap editors and already allows attachments in\nchats — including **registration-less live chats** where anonymous guests (U25\ncontext, minors) can send files to counsellors. Files must not be openable until\nchecked for viruses and harmful content (nudity, abuse imagery). Requirements\nfrom the planning session:"},"681":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"A file that has not passed checks must \"just sit there\" — not openable, and\nenforcement must not rely on client goodwill."},"682":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"Blur-until-checked thumbnails in the UI, driven by a queryable status\n(*unchecked / safe / blocked*)."},"683":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"Short-term a PoC using an AI API; long-term the option to swap in a\nself-hosted vision model must stay open."},"684":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"The whole capability must be toggleable through the ORISO settings cascade."},"685":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#context","content":"Matrix crypto is currently off (facade always-on), so the server side can see\nmedia content — server-side scanning is feasible today."},"686":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#options","content":"**A — matrix-content-scanner (chosen).** The official Element project that\nproxies media downloads: a client receives a file only after the scanner has\ncleared it. The actual check is an exchangeable script — ours chains ClamAV\n(virus) and a Mistral vision check (nudity/harmful). Denial is enforced at the\ndownload path, so an unchecked or failed file is server-side inaccessible\nregardless of client behaviour. Supports encrypted media via key-forwarding if\ncrypto is enabled later (chat rebuild epic)."},"687":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#options","content":"**B — custom scan service.** Own microservice notified on upload, status table,\nown status endpoint; every client must honour the status itself. More code, and\nenforcement is weaker: anyone with the mxc URL bypasses it."},"688":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"Deploy **matrix-content-scanner** as its own service in ORISO-Helm with a custom\nscan script: ClamAV first, then the AI check (Mistral API for the PoC — EU\nprovider, zero-retention, recorded as sub-processor in the KDG/AVV\ndocumentation)."},"689":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"Two hard properties:"},"690":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"**Fail-closed.** If any check is unreachable, errors, or is unsure, the file\nstays quarantined. Nothing is ever released \"in doubt\"."},"691":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"**The scan script is the exchange point.** Swapping Mistral for a self-hosted\nvision model later changes only the script, nothing else in the pipeline."},"692":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#decision","content":"Client blur state feeds from scanner verdicts: *not yet scanned* → blurred,\n*clean* → clear, *failed* → blocked tile. Before the pipeline exists, guest\nimages are blurred with counsellor click-to-reveal — the same state model with a\nhuman verdict."},"693":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#consequences","content":"Server-enforced quarantine for free; no per-client enforcement drift."},"694":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#consequences","content":"Scan-on-download adds latency on first open of a file; mitigated by scanning\neagerly and caching verdicts (scanner behaviour)."},"695":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#consequences","content":"Mistral becomes a KDG/AVV-documented sub-processor until self-hosting lands."},"696":{"id":"/decisions/adr-019-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-019","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-019#consequences","content":"If Matrix E2E encryption is enabled later, the scanner's encrypted-media\nsupport must be wired into the clients (key forwarding) — tracked in the chat\nrebuild epic, not here."},"697":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"page","content":"ADR-020: Scheduled calls, secure invitations, and a unified contact calendar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020"},"698":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"Status: Accepted — 2026-08-12 · Datum: 2026-08-12"},"699":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"Context"},"700":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#decision","content":"Decision"},"701":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#1-separate-appointment-call-session-and-call-invitation","content":"1\\. Separate Appointment, Call Session, and Call Invitation"},"702":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"2\\. Make call access a tenant policy enforced by the backend"},"703":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"3\\. Use one entry composition for QR, copied links, registered users, and guests"},"704":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"4\\. Provide one contact calendar across modalities"},"705":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"5\\. Model availability blockers and conflict deadlines explicitly"},"706":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#6-turn-the-conversation-projection-into-a-real-future-timeline","content":"6\\. Turn the conversation projection into a real Future Timeline"},"707":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"7\\. Distinguish persistent entry links from live-call invitations"},"708":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#8-use-versioned-call-timing-presets","content":"8\\. Use versioned call-timing presets"},"709":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#9-preserve-confidentiality-in-external-calendar-data","content":"9\\. Preserve confidentiality in external calendar data"},"710":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Bounded-context ownership"},"711":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Considered options (rejected)"},"712":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"713":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Required implementation slices"},"714":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"**Status:** Accepted — 2026-08-12"},"715":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"**Date:** 2026-08-12"},"716":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + architecture refinement session"},"717":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"**Related:** ADR-006 (persisted conversation modality), ADR-012 (group occurrences and Future Timeline), ADR-018 in ORISO-Frontend (Element Call Matryoshka integration), ORISO-Frontend#974"},"718":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020","content":"**Implementation tracker:** `OpenResilienceInitiative/ORISO-Frontend#974`"},"719":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"ORISO can already create appointments, export group occurrences to calendars, show a waiting-area countdown, and start encrypted Element Call rooms. These capabilities are not yet one coherent product:"},"720":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"audio and video conversations cannot consistently be offered as scheduled contacts;"},"721":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"the current appointment overview is a list rather than a useful calendar;"},"722":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"future appointments and group occurrences are projected in a basic expandable panel instead of a navigable future timeline;"},"723":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"the missing share action in an active call cannot safely be implemented as a plain room URL because call rooms are restricted and guest access is forbidden;"},"724":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"registration, login, QR entry, participant selection, and waiting-room components exist, but are not composed into one call-entry flow;"},"725":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"availability currently has only a coarse absence flag, so scheduled work needs real time ranges and deterministic conflict handling."},"726":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#context","content":"The design must support multiple contact types instead of creating a video-only calendar. It must also preserve the Matrix-only, encrypted Element Call architecture and avoid granting a call participant access to the source counselling conversation."},"727":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#1-separate-appointment-call-session-and-call-invitation","content":"An **Appointment** is the scheduled contact and its lifecycle. A **Call Session** is the runtime audio/video room materialized when a counsellor starts a planned or spontaneous call. A **Call Invitation** grants one identity access to exactly one Call Session."},"728":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#1-separate-appointment-call-session-and-call-invitation","content":"Planned and spontaneous calls use the same Call Session and invitation model. Scheduling does not pre-create a long-lived Matrix room. The appointment references its source conversation and intended participants; the restricted encrypted call room is created at call start."},"729":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"Each tenant selects one of two policies in ORISO Admin:"},"730":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"`REGISTERED_ONLY` — every participant must authenticate as a registered ORISO user;"},"731":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"`REGISTERED_OR_ONE_TIME_GUEST` — registered users are preferred, while a counsellor may also issue a one-time guest invitation."},"732":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"`REGISTERED_ONLY` is the secure default. The backend authorizes invitation creation and redemption; hiding a frontend action is not enforcement."},"733":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"A registered participant is selected through a compact reusable user picker. The participant receives membership only in the dedicated call room, never in the source case or chat room."},"734":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"A one-time guest passes through a modular pre-call identity screen derived from the existing registration/login flow. The resulting short-lived identity is bound to one invitation and one Call Session. It may reconnect during that call, expires when the call ends, and can be revoked by an authorized counsellor. Tokens are stored hashed and audit data never contains the usable secret."},"735":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#2-make-call-access-a-tenant-policy-enforced-by-the-backend","content":"All entry and exit events remain visible to participants. There is no per-person waiting-room approval in this first decision: a valid authenticated or one-time identity enters directly."},"736":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"An invitation URL or QR code opens a call-entry route that:"},"737":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"validates the invitation and tenant policy server-side;"},"738":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"offers login when the invitee already has an account;"},"739":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"offers the one-time identity flow only when tenant policy permits it;"},"740":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"shows the existing waiting-area countdown when the scheduled start is in the future;"},"741":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"joins the restricted Element Call room when the session is open."},"742":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#3-use-one-entry-composition-for-qr-copied-links-registered-users-and-guests","content":"The entry UI is a modular overlay or preceding screen, not a second registration implementation."},"743":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"The existing **Termine/Bookings** area becomes ORISO's unified **Contact Calendar**. It projects:"},"744":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"ordinary appointments;"},"745":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"planned audio calls;"},"746":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"planned video calls;"},"747":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"recurring and one-off group occurrences."},"748":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-50","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"Counsellors always have the calendar navigation entry. An advice seeker sees it only when at least one relevant appointment exists; self-booking starts inside the relevant conversation."},"749":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-51","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"Counsellors may create or propose appointments. Advice seekers may select a free slot from the conversation. A personal **Auto-confirmation Lead Time** controls approval:"},"750":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-52","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"a request made at least the configured duration before its start is confirmed automatically;"},"751":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-53","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"a request inside that window requires counsellor approval;"},"752":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-54","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"an already confirmed appointment never becomes approval-required merely because time passes."},"753":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-55","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#4-provide-one-contact-calendar-across-modalities","content":"The calendar is backed by a server-owned read projection rather than frontend joins between unrelated APIs. Each item exposes a stable identifier, time range, modality, status, source reference, permitted actions, and confidentiality-safe display data."},"754":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-56","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"Counsellors can create **Availability Blockers** as date/time ranges or all-day absences. Saving a blocker that overlaps confirmed appointments is allowed after a warning and creates explicit conflicts."},"755":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-57","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"The counsellor resolves affected appointments by the earlier of:"},"756":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-58","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"blocker creation time plus the personal **Conflict Resolution Deadline**; or"},"757":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-59","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"appointment start minus 15 minutes."},"758":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-60","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#5-model-availability-blockers-and-conflict-deadlines-explicitly","content":"The personal deadline is configured under **Profile → Appointment Settings**, defaults to one week, and cannot be shorter than 15 minutes. The first conflicting blocker may prompt the counsellor to confirm or change that setting. Unresolved conflicts are automatically cancelled at the effective deadline, with normal participant notification and an auditable reason."},"759":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-61","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#6-turn-the-conversation-projection-into-a-real-future-timeline","content":"The conversation list remains anchored at **Now** / the latest past event. A draggable divider reveals future events below it; the header shows the selected date or distance from today. Keyboard and explicit-button alternatives provide the same function without dragging."},"760":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-62","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#6-turn-the-conversation-projection-into-a-real-future-timeline","content":"Appointments and group occurrences use one typed future-event card/session primitive. Existing bounded loading from ADR-012 remains: the client must not materialize an unbounded future. Appointment-only users must see the projection even when no group series exists."},"761":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-63","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"ORISO supports three persistent link purposes:"},"762":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-64","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"**Conversation Link** — starts or opens a conversation;"},"763":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-65","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"**Video Appointment Link** — opens video-appointment booking;"},"764":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-66","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"**Smart Link** — offers conversation or audio/video appointment according to tenant and counsellor settings."},"765":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-67","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#7-distinguish-persistent-entry-links-from-live-call-invitations","content":"A persistent link never grants direct access to a live room. Direct live-call invitations are created only for a running Call Session and follow the identity-bound, revocable invitation rules above."},"766":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-68","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#8-use-versioned-call-timing-presets","content":"ORISO ships code-defined **Call Timing Presets**. A preset is a versioned sequence of actions relative to the scheduled end, for example a visual notice, an audible escalation, and an optional hard end. Presets may include a hard-end offset before or at the scheduled end; the product default is selected separately and is not implied by this ADR."},"767":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-69","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#8-use-versioned-call-timing-presets","content":"The counsellor selects a personal default under **Profile → Appointment Settings**. A running Element Call exposes a **Reminder** menu that may override the default for that Call Session. Tenants may restrict the offered preset set, but do not author arbitrary timing scripts."},"768":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-70","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#9-preserve-confidentiality-in-external-calendar-data","content":"ICS, Google Calendar, Outlook, email, and push projections contain no counselling topic, sensitive category, case text, or unnecessary provider branding. They use neutral appointment wording and an authenticated ORISO entry target."},"769":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-71","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Concern"},"770":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-72","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Owner"},"771":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-73","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Appointment lifecycle, availability, blockers, conflicts, unified calendar projection"},"772":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-74","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"ORISO-UserService at the ORISO boundary, integrating AppointmentService where required"},"773":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-75","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Tenant call-access policy and allowed timing presets"},"774":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-76","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"ORISO-TenantService"},"775":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-77","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Policy management UI"},"776":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-78","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"ORISO-Admin"},"777":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-79","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Calendar, Future Timeline, modular entry flow, participant picker, Element Call reminder UI"},"778":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-80","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"ORISO-Frontend"},"779":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-81","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"Restricted room membership and short-lived Matrix identity orchestration"},"780":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-82","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"ORISO-UserService with Matrix/Keycloak adapters"},"781":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-83","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#bounded-context-ownership","content":"No frontend-only flag may decide access to a call."},"782":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-84","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Make the existing restricted Matrix room link shareable as-is."},"783":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-85","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Create a public call room or enable unrestricted Matrix guests."},"784":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-86","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Add a video-only calendar beside existing appointments."},"785":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-87","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Pre-create a permanent call room for every future appointment."},"786":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-88","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Add one bespoke registration form inside Element Call."},"787":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-89","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Let the frontend aggregate appointments, group occurrences, absences, and permissions as the canonical model."},"788":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-90","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Model absences only as a boolean or silently delete conflicting appointments."},"789":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-91","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#considered-options-rejected","content":"Give tenants a free-form rules engine for call-ending behavior."},"790":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-92","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#consequences","content":"**Positive:** One model covers spontaneous and planned calls, registered and permitted guest participants, all contact modalities, and both calendar surfaces. Existing registration, picker, waiting-area, timer, group-occurrence, and Element Call components can be reused. Security is stronger than a copied room URL and is centrally enforceable."},"791":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-93","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#consequences","content":"**Cost / risk:** The work spans four repositories and the external AppointmentService boundary. Short-lived identities require cleanup and audit behavior. Calendar projection, conflict deadlines, notifications, and hard call termination need idempotent server jobs. Accessibility and mobile interaction for the draggable timeline require explicit alternatives and real-device validation."},"792":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-94","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Contracts and migrations: access policy, link purposes, appointments/modalities, availability blockers, conflict deadlines, timing preset identifiers, and the calendar read model."},"793":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-95","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Backend authorization: registered invitations, one-time identity issuance/redemption/revocation, room-scoped membership, expiry, audit, and cleanup."},"794":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-96","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Admin policy: secure defaults, tenant policy selection, preset allowlist, validation, and audit visibility."},"795":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-97","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Frontend primitives in Storybook: responsive Contact Calendar, event card, participant picker dialog, modular pre-call identity screen, waiting/countdown states, reminder menu, and accessible Future Timeline divider."},"796":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-98","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Appointment creation and self-booking: counsellor proposal, conversation-scoped booking, lead-time approval, availability blockers, conflict resolution, and notifications."},"797":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-99","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Element Call integration: scheduled and spontaneous session start, direct entry, reconnect, revoke, entry/exit notices, timing escalation, and optional hard end."},"798":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-100","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Persistent link purposes and Smart Link landing route."},"799":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-101","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Real-browser acceptance on mobile and desktop, including two-party bidirectional audio/video, registered-only denial, permitted one-time guest entry, room isolation, calendar visibility, timeline navigation, reconnect/revoke, and deadline jobs."},"800":{"id":"/decisions/adr-020-102","page_id":"/decisions/adr-020","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-020#required-implementation-slices","content":"Each slice is independently reviewable and follows red-green tests, repository quality gates, contract/integration coverage, Storybook visual review, and Playwright verification. A green UI test or pre-created room is not media proof; call acceptance requires bidirectional remote audio/video."},"801":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"page","content":"ADR-021: Legal-text hierarchy, generic versioning, and the consent text as a field of the DPP","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021"},"802":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-08-16"},"803":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021#context","content":"Context"},"804":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Measured current state (2026-08-16, `origin/pre-dev` unless noted)"},"805":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"Decision"},"806":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"807":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-021#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"808":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session)"},"809":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"**Date:** 2026-08-16"},"810":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"811":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"**Related:** `ADR-003` (Department = Agency × Topic carries imprint + DPP) and `ADR-014`\n(shared legal-text objects, topic-before-consent) — **both extended by this ADR, neither\nsuperseded**; `ADR-022` (consent gates in counselling sessions — the runtime half of this\ndecision); `ADR-023` (platform-to-Träger governance); `CONTEXT-legal-documents.md`;\n`PLAN-dsfa-living-document-2026-08-13.md`"},"812":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021","content":"**Scope note:** this ADR is about the *documents*. When they are shown, and how a help-seeker's\nagreement is recorded, is `ADR-022`. What the platform and a Träger sign between themselves is\n`ADR-023`."},"813":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#context","content":"ADR-003 and ADR-014 established that a Department (Agency × Topic) carries its own imprint and\ndata-protection policy (DPP), and that legal texts should be shareable objects rather than\nduplicated inline strings. Both are correct and remain in force. Neither describes the **complete\nladder of levels**, and neither addresses **versioning** or the **consent sentence** that a\nhelp-seeker actually ticks."},"814":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#context","content":"That gap produced repeated, expensive confusion — most visibly a trivial live-chat modal bug that\nwas re-diagnosed three times because nobody could state which document applies at which point in\nthe flow."},"815":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**Four levels exist, not the two or three usually assumed:**"},"816":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"#"},"817":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Level"},"818":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Storage"},"819":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Fields"},"820":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"1"},"821":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Platform operator"},"822":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"\"main tenant\" under single-domain multitenancy, `SingleDomainTenantOverrideService`"},"823":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`contentImpressum`, `contentPrivacy`"},"824":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"2"},"825":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Träger (tenant)"},"826":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`tenant`"},"827":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"same two, plus `contentPrivacyActivationDate`"},"828":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"3"},"829":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Beratungsstelle (agency)"},"830":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`agency`"},"831":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`contentDpp`, `contentImprint` (agency-wide, deliberately without publication status)"},"832":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"4"},"833":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Fachbereich (Department = agency × topic)"},"834":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`agency_topic`"},"835":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"`contentDpp`, `contentImprint`, each with its own publication status"},"836":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"Resolution runs upward: `DepartmentLegalService` takes the published department text, else the\nagency-wide text (lines 65–66 / 75–76). Level 1 versus level 2 is decided by the application\nsetting `legalContentChangesBySingleTenantAdminsAllowed`; when it is on, a Träger **replaces** the\nplatform text rather than adding to it."},"837":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**There is no version history for legal texts.** `legal_text` carries only\n`publication_status` DRAFT/PUBLISHED and no archive table. The only versioned legal object in the\nwhole system is the AVV (`tenant_dpa_version`, TenantService changeset 0018, endpoint\n`/tenantadmin/{id}/dpa/versions`). Publishing a new DPP or imprint overwrites the previous wording\nwithout trace — so today no Träger can prove which policy was in force on a given date."},"838":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**The editor already supports versions; only the data source is missing.** `M3RichTextEditor`\nimplements the full version UI (selection, \"online since\", \"adopt as new draft\", comparison), but\nits `versions` prop is populated exclusively by `DataProcessingAgreementCard`. `LegalText/index.tsx`\nand `DepartmentDataProtectionCard` use the same component without version data, and the Admin API\nlayer has only `getDpaVersions.ts`."},"839":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**The consent sentence is static frontend i18n.** It is assembled from three fragments\n(`registration.dataProtection.label.{prefix,and,suffix}` in `AccountData.tsx`) around the legal\nlinks. No backend involvement, no configurability. A `LegalConsentTemplateEditor` exists in the\nPlaceholderTemplate module with `{{Beratungsstelle}}`, `{{Thema}}`, `{{legal_links}}` tokens — as a\nStorybook component without a backing feature."},"840":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**Inheritance is asymmetric.** Department → agency is resolved server-side by\n`DepartmentLegalService`; → Träger happens client-side (Admin `mergeTranslatedContent`, Frontend\n`pickConsentPrivacyContent`)."},"841":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev-unless-noted","content":"**Additional constraints found:** `legal_text.kind` is a free `varchar(20)` with no CHECK\nconstraint; `/agencies/{id}/topics/{tid}/legal` returns raw, unrendered text (no Freemarker on that\npath, so placeholders reach the browser verbatim); the existing backend renderer is Freemarker,\nwhere `${...}` can invoke object methods."},"842":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**The ladder has four levels and the platform level is named.** Platform operator → Träger →\nBeratungsstelle → Fachbereich, resolved bottom-up with fallback. Any document reference in code,\ntickets, or UI states its level. \"The privacy policy\" without a level is not a valid statement."},"843":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**Replacing is sufficient; the guarantee moves into validation.** A Träger text replaces the\nplatform text rather than being appended to it. One sentence, one checkbox. What protects the\nplatform's mandatory disclosures is **not** a legal stacking rule but a technical one: a consent\ntext **cannot be published** unless it contains the `{{legal_links}}` token — validated\nserver-side with an editor error — and the cookie/authentication notice is rendered as a fixed,\nnon-editable addendum beneath the sentence."},"844":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**A generic legal-text version history is built**, for DPP, imprint, and future kinds, on all\nlevels. The AVV mechanism (`tenant_dpa_version`) is the blueprint; this is copying, not\ninventing. A generic mechanism is *less* work than a special case for the DPP alone — same\ntable, same endpoint, same editor wiring, distinguished by kind. It also closes a standing\ncompliance gap."},"845":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**The consent text is a field of the data-protection policy, not its own legal-text kind.**\nChanging the consent wording means publishing a new DPP version whose body text may be\nunchanged. This yields one history instead of two, and makes \"which consent belonged to which\npolicy\" trivially answerable (same version) instead of reconstructed from timestamps — timestamp\ncorrelation was already a defect source in the AVV work (second precision versus MariaDB\n`DATETIME(0)`)."},"846":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**Placeholder substitution is split by who owns the data.** The server substitutes what it\nknows (`{{Beratungsstelle}}`, `{{Thema}}`, contact data); the client substitutes\n`{{legal_links}}` with the real, clickable links, because those come from the frontend\ndeployment configuration (`LegalLinksProvider` / `settings.legalLinks`) and the backend does not\nknow them."},"847":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**Token syntax is `{{key}}`, never Freemarker `${key}`.** Träger-authored text must never pass\nthrough Freemarker: `${...}` can call object methods there, which makes tenant-authored content a\ntemplate-injection surface. A plain `{{key}}` replacement cannot do that by construction. The\nproduct consequently carries two dialects — `${}` for the existing DPP placeholders\n(`responsible`, `dataProtectionOfficer`), `{{}}` for mails and the consent text. Unifying them is\na separate concern, deliberately deferred."},"848":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**The imprint is an information duty and never a consent gate.** It requires guaranteed\nreachability on every level; it is never ticked, never blocks, and never triggers re-consent.\nOnly the DPP (and, between platform and Träger, the documents in ADR-023) are consent-bearing."},"849":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**The platform template and the platform's own governing document are separate objects.** The\ntemplate that pre-fills a Träger's consent text carries no legal force; the main tenant's own\nDPP governs whenever no Träger is resolved. Editing the template must never change the document\nin force for unassigned visitors."},"850":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#decision","content":"**Inheritance becomes server-side end to end.** The department → agency → Träger → platform\nchain resolves in one place on the server. The present client-side half (Admin\n`mergeTranslatedContent`, Frontend `pickConsentPrivacyContent`) is a defect source that the\nconsent text would otherwise inherit."},"851":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#consequences","content":"**Positive:** every legal document has a resolvable level and a provable history; the \"which text\napplied when\" question becomes answerable for the first time; the consent sentence becomes a Träger\nresponsibility without the platform losing its mandatory disclosures; one version pointer covers\nboth the policy and its consent wording (see ADR-022); the existing editor UI is reused as-is."},"852":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-50","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** an archive table plus endpoints per legal-text kind; a validation path for the\nmandatory token; the client-side inheritance half has to be moved server-side; two token dialects\ncoexist until a later unification; the Admin needs version selection wired onto the legal-text cards\nthat already support it."},"853":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-51","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#alternatives-considered","content":"**Append the Träger text to the platform sentence, or show two checkboxes.** Rejected: two\ndocuments governing the same processing eventually contradict each other, and two ticks is a worse\nuser experience. Liability is instead secured by decision 2."},"854":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-52","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#alternatives-considered","content":"**`legal_text.kind = CONSENT` as its own object with its own `consent_id` slots.** Migration-free\n(the column has no constraint), but requires a second version history and extends four OpenAPI\nenums, and reintroduces the correlation problem decision 4 removes."},"855":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-53","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#alternatives-considered","content":"**Version history for the DPP only.** Rejected: more work than the generic mechanism, and leaves\nthe imprint gap open."},"856":{"id":"/decisions/adr-021-54","page_id":"/decisions/adr-021","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-021#alternatives-considered","content":"**Substitution entirely client-side or entirely server-side.** Client-only cannot reach agency\ncontact data and breaks email/PDF renderings of the same text; server-only would require migrating\nthe link targets out of the frontend deployment configuration."},"857":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"page","content":"ADR-022: Two consent gates, consent state as a session pointer, and re-consent on change","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022"},"858":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-08-16"},"859":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022#context","content":"Context"},"860":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"Measured current state (2026-08-16, `origin/pre-dev`)"},"861":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"Decision"},"862":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"863":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"864":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session)"},"865":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"**Date:** 2026-08-16"},"866":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"867":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"**Related:** `ADR-021` (the documents themselves — read first); `ADR-014` (topic-before-consent\ninvariant); `ADR-007` (live-chat availability; the waiting room is decoupled from counsellor\navailability); `ADR-023` (platform ↔ Träger); ORISO-UserService #927 (anonymous consent gate);\n`CONTEXT-legal-documents.md`"},"868":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022","content":"**Scope:** sessions that have a **help-seeker** — 1:1 counselling, live chat, self-help groups.\nInternal rooms (supervision per ADR-008, Team-Besprechung per ADR-016) have no help-seeker and\ntherefore no consent gate."},"869":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#context","content":"The live chat runs in two legally distinct phases, and conflating them has repeatedly produced\nbugs that looked like frontend defects."},"870":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#context","content":"**Phase 1 — waiting room.** The help-seeker rolls a display name, picks a topic, and waits.\nPractically nothing is stored: a cookie and a temporary password. No Beratungsstelle is assigned\nyet, so no Beratungsstelle document can apply. What *does* apply is the platform-level policy —\nprocessing begins the moment the page is opened (IP, cookies, name generation, topic selection),\nexactly as a general policy applies to any site visitor before registration. Clicking \"join waiting\nroom\" is the agreement to that. Leaving the waiting room leaves nothing behind."},"871":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#context","content":"**Phase 2 — a counsellor accepts.** Only now is the help-seeker routed to a Beratungsstelle, which\nhas its own imprint and DPP. That document must be agreed to before the conversation starts."},"872":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#context","content":"Anonymity in this model is a property of the **read-only display name plus generated password**,\nnot of the chat content. As long as the display name cannot be edited, the platform can state in the\nDPIA that the help-seeker is anonymous **up to the point of entering the chat**. What someone\nsubsequently writes into the room is outside the platform's control and deliberately not its\nconcern."},"873":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`CreateUserFacade:303–304` deliberately nulls `dataPrivacyConfirmation` and\n`termsAndConditionsConfirmation` for the anonymous account. This is **correct** for phase 1 —\nthere is no Beratungsstelle document to have agreed to — and was repeatedly misread as a bug."},"874":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"Staleness is decided by comparing the user timestamp against `tenant.contentPrivacyActivationDate`\n— a tenant-wide date with no reference to which document or which version."},"875":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`TermsAndConditions.tsx` suppresses its update modal via `isAnonymousAsker`, which tests\n`userName.startsWith('Anonymous-')`. Generated names look like `anon_8`, so the test is false and\nthe modal fires in the waiting room, where there is nothing to update. The WEITER button in that\nmodal issues no request at all — a dead end that also affects registered users."},"876":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`isDisplayNameEditable` is a **Träger** setting and reads `false` for anonymous and registered\naccounts alike. It cannot be used to identify an individual anonymous account."},"877":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`Session` has **no consent field of any kind**."},"878":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`AnonymousEnquiryConsentGuard` blocks assignment server-side (on `origin/pre-dev`; absent from a\nstale detached-HEAD checkout, which is why it appears missing locally)."},"879":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`AnonymousConsentGate` renders `consentLabelHtml` through `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` **without a\nsanitizer** — harmless while the input is i18n text, a real hole once Träger-authored text lands\nthere."},"880":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#measured-current-state-2026-08-16-originpre-dev","content":"`CreateSessionFacade` knows two rules: `ONE_SESSION_PER_CONSULTING_TYPE` (active at all three call\nsites) and `ONE_SESSION_PER_TOPIC_ID_AND_AGENCY_ID` (implemented as\n`checkIfAlreadyRegisteredToTopicAndSameAgency`, **never passed by any caller**). Today a\nhelp-seeker therefore cannot open a second counselling session on the same topic with a *different*\nBeratungsstelle — which would force them into a second account."},"881":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Exactly two gates, no third.**"},"882":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Gate 1, entering the waiting room:** the platform-level policy (or the Träger's replacement,\nwhen a Träger is already resolved — see ADR-021 decision 2). One document, one agreement."},"883":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Gate 2, in the room before the first message:** the Beratungsstelle / Fachbereich document.\n`AnonymousConsentGate` is that gate; ORISO-UserService #927 **is** stage 2, not an addition to\nit. Placing it inside the room rather than in front of the door is equivalent in substance and\nis already backed server-side by `AnonymousEnquiryConsentGuard`."},"884":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Consent state is a pointer on the session, not a consent log.** `session` gains a nullable\n`consented_legal_version_id` referencing the legal-text version the room is cleared for. It is\n**overwritten** on re-consent; no append-only history, no per-user audit trail, no behavioural\nrecord. The referenced target is a public document version, so this adds no new category of\npersonal data. Because ADR-021 decision 4 attaches the consent wording to the DPP, this single\npointer covers both."},"885":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Proof of what applied is carried by the publication history, not by a user log.** \"Which\nwording was in force from when to when\" is answered by the version history from ADR-021 decision\n3\\. Since no session can proceed without the gate, agreement to the then-current text follows.\nThe obligation sits with the Träger / Beratungsstelle, not in a record about anonymous\nhelp-seekers. Decision 2 exists for **control flow** — knowing whether to open the composer —\nnot as evidence."},"886":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**A changed text notifies inside the chat; continuing to write is the agreement.** When a\nBeratungsstelle publishes a new version, the affected rooms receive a system notification stating\nthat the policy has changed, carrying the permanent link to it, and stating plainly that\ncontinuing the conversation constitutes agreement and that anyone who does not agree should stop.\nReading the history is never blocked — sealing a counselling transcript would be irresponsible."},"887":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**Substantive changes require an explicit act.*&#x2A; The legal editor carries a per-version flag\n&#x2A;*\"new consent required\"**, set by the publisher. Unset (the normal case, and the default) yields\nthe flow in decision 4. Set, the same notification becomes a Yes/No control that blocks *sending*\nuntil answered, reusing the existing frontend yes/no pattern. Rationale: a data-protection policy\nis primarily an information duty, and silent continuation is adequate for wording, addresses, and\nclarifications. It is not adequate where the **scope or legal basis** of processing changes — a\nnew data category, a new recipient, new analysis. GDPR Art. 4(11) requires an unambiguous\naffirmative act there, and counselling data falls under Art. 9. Only the publishing body knows\nwhich case it is, so only it can set the flag."},"888":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**A help-seeker may hold sessions with several Beratungsstellen on one account.**\n`ONE_SESSION_PER_TOPIC_ID_AND_AGENCY_ID` is activated at the call sites in place of\n`ONE_SESSION_PER_CONSULTING_TYPE`. Forcing a second account is the worse outcome: it breaks the\nanonymity statement, the statistics, and the retention windows."},"889":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#decision","content":"**A topic collision is a notice, never a block.** When a help-seeker opens a second session on a\ntopic they already have open elsewhere, the **older** chat receives a friendly system note that\nanother conversation on this topic exists. Neither the other Beratungsstelle nor the time is\nnamed, so anonymity is untouched — but the counsellor can see why and ask. This is secondary\nscope, not a blocker for decision 6."},"890":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#consequences","content":"**Positive:** the waiting-room modal bug class disappears by construction, because a room that has\nno Beratungsstelle assigned has nothing to update; no anonymity detection is needed anywhere, so no\ncode has to guess from display names; two Beratungsstellen mean two independent consent states, and a\nchange at one does not disturb the other; the second-account workaround is removed; data minimisation\nis preserved because no per-user consent trail is created."},"891":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** one nullable column plus a write path; the notification and the Yes/No branch\nhave to be built in the chat; activating the finer session constraint permits parallel counselling\non the same topic at two bodies, which is a professional matter, not a data-model one; the topic\nnotice needs the event/notification subsystem (feasibility to be verified before ticketing)."},"892":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#consequences","content":"**Blocking dependency:** `AnonymousConsentGate` must be routed through the existing\n`LegalContentRenderer` sanitizer *before* Träger-authored text is delivered to it. Gate 2 cannot ship\nwith an unsanitised `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`."},"893":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"**Detect anonymity in the frontend and suppress the modal.** Rejected — it is the wrong predicate.\nThe condition is \"is this session already assigned to a Beratungsstelle\", which needs no anonymity\ndetection at all."},"894":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"**Store the phase-1 agreement into `dataPrivacyConfirmation` at account creation.** Rejected — it\nwould satisfy the stale comparison and thereby *skip* gate 2, which is worse than the bug."},"895":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"**A per-user consent event log (who agreed to which version when).** Rejected — it creates a\nbehavioural record about anonymous help-seekers that does not exist today, for evidentiary value\nthe publication history already provides. Decision 2 keeps only the state needed to run the flow."},"896":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"**Always require an explicit Yes/No on any change.** Rejected — every typo would trigger a consent\nwave across all running counselling sessions."},"897":{"id":"/decisions/adr-022-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-022","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-022#alternatives-considered","content":"**Block a second session on the same topic.** Rejected — it produces second accounts, which is the\noutcome with the worst privacy properties."},"898":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","type":"page","content":"ADR-023: The Platform Services Agreement, living templates, and proportionate escalation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-023"},"899":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-0","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"Status: Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session) · Datum: 2026-08-16"},"900":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-1","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-023#context","content":"Context"},"901":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-2","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Decision"},"902":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-3","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-023#consequences","content":"Consequences"},"903":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-4","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"Alternatives considered"},"904":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-5","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"**Status:** Accepted — Frank, 2026-08-16 (grill-with-docs session)"},"905":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-6","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"**Date:** 2026-08-16"},"906":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-7","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"**Deciders:** Frank (product) + AI (engineering)"},"907":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-8","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"**Related:** `ADR-021` (legal-text hierarchy and versioning); `ADR-022` (help-seeker consent);\nEPIC AVV / DPA work (`ADR-003` era, `tenant_dpa_version`, `DpaLegalForm`);\n`PLAN-dsfa-living-document-2026-08-13.md` section 7.6 (proportionality of compliance\nescalations); `CONTEXT-legal-documents.md`"},"908":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-9","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023","content":"**Scope:** the relationship between the **platform operator** and a **Träger**. The help-seeker\ndoes not appear in this ADR."},"909":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-10","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#context","content":"The admin module presents the Auftragsverarbeitungsvertrag (AVV) as if it were the whole agreement\nbetween platform operator and Träger. It is not — it is one annex. Alongside it sit the service\nterms, the technical and organisational measures, the subprocessor list, and references to further\ndocuments such as the DPIA. A Träger signing \"the AVV\" is in fact concluding a contract of which the\nAVV is one part, and the module both mis-names and under-shows what is being signed."},"910":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-11","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#context","content":"Separately, ADR-021 introduces a platform template that pre-fills a Träger's consent text. A\ntemplate without a maintained connection to its origin is a copy: legal corrections made centrally\nnever reach the Träger who copied it a year earlier."},"911":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-12","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#context","content":"And once the platform can require a Träger to adopt something, the question of what happens on\nrefusal becomes a product decision with safety consequences. ORISO carries U25 suicide prevention;\nan enforcement mechanism that terminates counselling would endanger the very people the\ndata-protection rule exists to protect."},"912":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-13","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**The agreement is named as a contract, and the AVV is an annex to it.**"},"913":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-14","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"German (UI, Träger-facing)"},"914":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-15","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"English (code, ADRs, GitHub)"},"915":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-16","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"The whole"},"916":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-17","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**Plattformvertrag**"},"917":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-18","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**Platform Services Agreement**"},"918":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-19","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Annex 1"},"919":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-20","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Auftragsverarbeitungsvertrag (AVV), Art. 28 GDPR"},"920":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-21","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Data Processing Agreement (DPA)"},"921":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-22","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Annex 2"},"922":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-23","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Technische und organisatorische Maßnahmen (TOM), Art. 32"},"923":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-24","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Technical and Organisational Measures"},"924":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-25","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Annex 3"},"925":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-26","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Unterauftragsverarbeiter"},"926":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-27","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Subprocessor list"},"927":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-28","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Annex 4"},"928":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-29","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Leistungsbeschreibung / Nutzungsbedingungen"},"929":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-30","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Service description / terms of use"},"930":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-31","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Alongside"},"931":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-32","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"Verweise (DSFA, Datenschutzerklärung der Plattform)"},"932":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-33","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"References — linked, not co-signed"},"933":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-34","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"The act is **Vertragsabschluss**; the record is an **Unterzeichnung** carrying signing date,\nsigning person, and their role. \"Vereinbarung\" is not used: a Träger concludes a binding contract\nby clicking, and the wording should say so. In English, \"Agreement\" is the standard binding term\nand is kept. Entities read `platform_agreement`, `agreement_annex`, `agreement_signature`."},"934":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-35","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"This renames and re-frames an existing module; it does not change who signs what. Existing AVV\ntickets are **renamed**, not replaced."},"935":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-36","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**The platform template keeps a living connection to its origin.**"},"936":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-37","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"A Träger text records **which template version** it was derived from. This costs nothing extra,\nbecause ADR-021 decision 3 gives the template versions anyway."},"937":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-38","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"When the platform operator publishes a new template version, every Träger text with an older\nreference is automatically \"outdated\" — a number comparison, not a notification system."},"938":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-39","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"The Admin shows a hint with a **side-by-side comparison**. Adopting means the Träger publishes\ntheir own new version containing the changes; declining clears the hint."},"939":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-40","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"The existing \"new from template\" split button in the PlaceholderTemplate module is exactly this\nmechanism."},"940":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-41","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**The template and the platform's own governing document are separate objects.** A template is a\npattern with no legal force; the main tenant's own DPP governs whenever no Träger is resolved.\nEditing a suggestion must never set law for unassigned visitors. (Also recorded as ADR-021\ndecision 8, because it constrains the data model there.)"},"941":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-42","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**Every template change is marked recommended or mandatory.** Only \"mandatory\" carries a\ndeadline. Cosmetic changes may be ignored without consequence; a change forced by law may not."},"942":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-43","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**Escalation is staged and has a hard limit.** If a Träger does not adopt a mandatory change by\nthe deadline: hint → warning banner → **suspension of new registrations** for that Träger."},"943":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-44","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#decision","content":"**Non-negotiable:** running counselling sessions, logins of existing help-seekers, and access to\nexisting histories are **always** preserved. Data-protection enforcement must never endanger the\nprotected interest it exists to serve. The model is the existing AVV gate, which hard-blocks only\nthe creation of new Beratungsstellen and otherwise warns. This principle applies platform-wide and\nanswers GDPR Art. 35(7)(d) (remedies including safeguards for data subjects); it is recorded as\nsection 7.6 of the DPIA plan."},"944":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-45","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#consequences","content":"**Positive:** a Träger sees what they are actually signing; central legal corrections reach every\nTräger without a push channel; the platform can enforce what the law requires without acquiring the\npower to cut off counselling; the naming stops implying that the AVV is the entire relationship."},"945":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-46","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#consequences","content":"**Negative / cost:** the admin module grows from one document to a contract with annexes; a\nderivation reference plus outdated detection plus a comparison view have to be built; the deadline\nand escalation logic is new; UI wording, ADR titles, entity names, and existing tickets have to be\nrenamed consistently in one pass."},"946":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-47","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Keep calling it \"Vereinbarung\".** Rejected — too weak for something concluded by clicking, and\nit obscures that the AVV is only one part."},"947":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-48","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Plain copy of the template with no connection.** Rejected — legal corrections would never reach\nthe Träger."},"948":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-49","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Template stays authoritative, the Träger only appends.** Rejected — contradicts ADR-021\ndecision 2 (one sentence, one checkbox)."},"949":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-50","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Warning only, no consequence.** Rejected — a Träger could indefinitely sit out something legally\nrequired."},"950":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-51","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Automatic adoption after the deadline.** Rejected — the Träger would have published a text they\nnever read."},"951":{"id":"/decisions/adr-023-52","page_id":"/decisions/adr-023","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions/adr-023#alternatives-considered","content":"**Suspending logins or terminating sessions on non-compliance.** Rejected outright; see decision 5."},"952":{"id":"/decisions","page_id":"/decisions","type":"page","content":"Architekturentscheidungen (ADR)","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Entscheidungen (ADR)"],"tags":[],"url":"/decisions"},"953":{"id":"/decisions-0","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Plattformweite Architecture Decision Records — 23 Entscheidungen, aus dem Repository ORISO-Docs."},"954":{"id":"/decisions-1","page_id":"/decisions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions#herkunft-und-pflege","content":"Herkunft und Pflege"},"955":{"id":"/decisions-2","page_id":"/decisions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions#decisions-authored-after-the-import","content":"Decisions authored after the import"},"956":{"id":"/decisions-3","page_id":"/decisions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions#known-issues","content":"Known issues"},"957":{"id":"/decisions-4","page_id":"/decisions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/decisions#other-local-adr-collections-not-imported-here","content":"Other local ADR collections NOT imported here"},"958":{"id":"/decisions-5","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Diese Reihe ist die kanonische Sammlung der plattformweiten Entscheidungen. Die DSFA-Kapitel verweisen auf sie; jeder Verweis der Form `ADR-0NN` in den Kapiteltexten ist auf die jeweilige Seite verlinkt."},"959":{"id":"/decisions-6","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Nr."},"960":{"id":"/decisions-7","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Entscheidung"},"961":{"id":"/decisions-8","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Status"},"962":{"id":"/decisions-9","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"ADR-001"},"963":{"id":"/decisions-10","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Counselling modalities as toggleable modules"},"964":{"id":"/decisions-11","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Proposed — needs a team decision (esp. how registration filt"},"965":{"id":"/decisions-12","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"ADR-002"},"966":{"id":"/decisions-13","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Silent room membership with an access-control confidentiality curtain (not E2EE)"},"967":{"id":"/decisions-14","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending)"},"968":{"id":"/decisions-15","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"ADR-003"},"969":{"id":"/decisions-16","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Department = unique (Agency × Topic) carrying its own imprint + DPP"},"970":{"id":"/decisions-17","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Accepted — Frank, 2026-06-25 (team ratification pending)"},"971":{"id":"/decisions-18","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"ADR-004"},"972":{"id":"/decisions-19","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Keep the custom chat UI; adopt matrix-js-sdk Megolm under it (don't embed Element Web)"},"973":{"id":"/decisions-20","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). June-30 sco"},"974":{"id":"/decisions-21","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"ADR-005"},"975":{"id":"/decisions-22","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Matrix federation deliberately OFF; real DNS server\\_name via a clean homeserver rebuild"},"976":{"id":"/decisions-23","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/decisions","content":"Accepted — 2026-06-26 (grill-with-docs session). Timing fixe"},"977":{"id":"/decisions-24","page_id":"/decisions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/de