e per-Träger editor, reusing the legal-texts editor and its machine translation)"],[1216,"Administrationsoberfläche"],[590,"Admins configure media behaviour per chat type like video calls — familiar UI,\nno new concepts."],[962,"ADR-001"],[11,"ADR-001: Counselling modalities as toggleable modules"],[965,"ADR-002"],[59,"ADR-002: Silent room membership with an access-control confidentiality curtain (not E2EE)"],[968,"ADR-003"],[813,"ADR-003 and ADR-014 established that a Department (Agency × Topic) carries its own imprint and\ndata-protection policy (DPP), and that legal texts should be shareable objects rather than\nduplicated inline strings. Both are correct and remain in force. Neither describes the **complete\nladder of levels**, and neither addresses **versioning** or the **consent sentence** that a\nhelp-seeker actually ticks."],[558,"ADR-003 correctly made the Department = unique (agency\\_id, topic\\_id) the carrier of the\nindividualised Impressum + DPP. But two of its implementation choices turned out to violate the\nresult the domain actually needs:"],[110,"ADR-003: Department = unique (Agency × Topic) carrying its own imprint + DPP"],[971,"ADR-004"],[143,"ADR-004: Keep the custom chat UI; adopt matrix-js-sdk Megolm under it (don't embed Element Web)"],[974,"ADR-005"],[520,"ADR-005 clean homeserver rebuild with stable DNS `server_name`."],[189,"ADR-005 is only partially applied. Federation hardening reached Pre-Dev, but the homeserver still uses the bare-IP `server_name`; the clean rebuild remains the hard blocker."],[492,"ADR-005 remains incomplete: federation hardening was partially hot-applied on Pre-Dev, but the homeserver still uses the bare-IP `server_name`; the clean rebuild remains an ops-owned blocker."],[203,"ADR-005: Matrix federation deliberately OFF; real DNS server_name via a clean homeserver rebuild"],[977,"ADR-006"],[489,"ADR-006 #410 now owns the cross-modality persistence and regression gate before promotion."],[249,"ADR-006: `conversation